  ('puerto-morelos-mexico', '10S', 'Puerto Morelos', 'Mexico', 'A reef 500 meters off a sleepy fishing dock', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Quintana Roo (Cancún & Riviera Maya)', '{"diveglobal","ocean","adventure","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier"}', null, 'core', '{"key_facts":["Puerto Morelos Reef National Park lies less than 500 m offshore, one of the best-preserved in the Caribbean","Juan Escutia boat is now an artificial reef; reef holds turtles, rays, nurse/bull sharks","Northern gateway to the ~17 km Route of the Cenotes (entry ~150-250 MXN each)","Deep-sea fishing for dorado, wahoo, tuna, barracuda","Runs ~20-30% cheaper than Playa del Carmen, 40-60% cheaper than Cancún Hotel Zone"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"town clinics; major trauma in Cancún (~36 km, Galenia/Hospiten - verify) or Playa del Carmen; hyperbaric via SSS Cancún / Cozumel","advisory_level":"L2","malaria":"none in QR tourist zones (verify); dengue precautions","yellow_fever":"none required","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua State of Sinaloa FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Dec-Apr (dry/high season; driest reef water, own rates peak)","shoulder":"May-Jun & Nov (~30-40% off winter, layered on structural ~20-30% vs Playa del Carmen)","green":"Jun-mid-Oct (hurricane season, ~40-60% off; reef/cenote year-round, dry-season visibility best)","booking_lead":"shoulder/green beds 2-4 wks; reef/cenote tours 1-3 wks; Dec-Apr beds + Zoëtry/Royalton Reserve ultra suite 3-6+ months (more for Christmas/NY)","off_season_specials":"double-discount play - ''cheaper than Cancún AND low season''; pair value bed with year-round national-park reef + weather-resilient Route of the Cenotes; disclose hurricane/sargassum","event_peaks":"Christmas-New Year, US spring break (Mar); no single marquee wildlife event - reef + cenotes are the year-round draw","campaign_start":"winter/value-vs-Cancún Aug-Sep; green-season ''cheaper base + cenotes'' Apr-May; ultra corridor (Mayakoba/Zoëtry) 6-9 months ahead"},"jewels":[{"name":"Juan Escutia wreck","si_tag":"diveglobal","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"sunken boat now an artificial reef and fish refuge","bookable_category":"guided reef/wreck dive","source":"https://www.kooxdiving.com/en/activities/diving-in-the-sea/puerto-morelos-reef-shipwreck-diving/","timing":"Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"sunken boat now an artificial reef and fish refuge","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"local dive-op → OTA affiliate"},{"name":"Puerto Morelos Reef National Park snorkel","si_tag":"ocean","status":"future","tier":"essential","hook":"living reef under 500 m offshore, turtles/rays/lobster","bookable_category":"guided reef snorkel/dive","source":"https://voyage-mexico.com/en/puerto-morelos.html","si":"ocean","blurb":"living reef under 500 m offshore, turtles/rays/lobster","commission":"local operator → OTA (park fee pass-through)"},{"name":"Deep-sea fishing charter","si_tag":"ocean","status":"future","tier":"premier","hook":"half/full-day for dorado, wahoo, tuna, barracuda","bookable_category":"private/shared charter","source":"https://voyage-mexico.com/en/puerto-morelos.html","timing":"Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"ocean","blurb":"half/full-day for dorado, wahoo, tuna, barracuda","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"local charter operator → curated-recommend"},{"name":"Route of the Cenotes","si_tag":"globaladv","status":"future","tier":"comfort","hook":"~17 km jungle road of open/semi-open/cave cenotes","bookable_category":"day tour + per-cenote entry","source":"https://snorkelingadventure.com/blog/snorkeling-puerto-morelos-cenotes-riviera-maya-adventure/","timing":"Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"adventure","blurb":"~17 km jungle road of open/semi-open/cave cenotes","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"DMC/local operator → OTA (entry pass-through)"},{"name":"Fishing-village seafood + craft market","si_tag":"culinary","status":"future","tier":"essential","hook":"fresh-off-the-boat ceviche + plaza craft market","bookable_category":"food/culture experience","source":"https://www.palladiumhotelgroup.com/en/travel-guides/mexico/riviera-maya/what-to-see/puerto-morelos","timing":"Dec-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","blurb":"fresh-off-the-boat ceviche + plaza craft market","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"curated-recommend (largely non-commissionable)"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Puerto Morelos?","a":"Sargassum, hurricanes and water — not crime. 2026 is heavy region-wide for sargassum, and Puerto Morelos'' open Caribbean-facing beaches are affected, so plan cenote and reef days as hedges; drink bottled water, use repellent for dengue (no malaria in the tourist zone), and note hurricane season runs June–November, September riskiest.","source":"howisthesargassum.com","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is Puerto Morelos good for diving and the Juan Escutia wreck?","a":"Yes — it is an underrated day-boat dive base. The Puerto Morelos Reef National Park sits under 500 m offshore, one of the Caribbean''s best-preserved reefs, and the sunken Juan Escutia is now an artificial reef and fish refuge steps away. Visibility is best in the dry Oct–March window; book in town, where it is cheaper and supports local operators.","source":"voyage-mexico.com","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Can I go deep-sea fishing from Puerto Morelos?","a":"Yes — it is a working fishing port, so charters are authentic and close at hand. Half- and full-day trips target dorado (mahi-mahi), wahoo, tuna and barracuda, with gear and guide included; the species mix is seasonal, so confirm with the operator. It pairs naturally with the fresh-off-the-boat ceviche at the beachfront cantinas.","source":"voyage-mexico.com","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"What is the Route of the Cenotes?","a":"A ~17 km jungle road of cenotes running inland from town — Puerto Morelos is its northern gateway. It strings together open, semi-open and cave cenotes for swimming, cavern diving and ziplining, at roughly 150–250 MXN entry each. Because they are shaded jungle sites, cenotes are weather-resilient — a strong rainy-day and green-season option.","source":"snorkelingadventure.com","si_tag":"globaladv"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Puerto Morelos, Mexico: Reef, Cenotes & Fishing Village","meta_description":"A quiet Riviera Maya port with a national-park reef 500 m offshore, the Juan Escutia wreck, and the Route of the Cenotes. Cheaper than Cancún — when and how to book.","slug":"puerto-morelos-mexico","primary_keyword":"Puerto Morelos reef diving","long_tail":["Puerto Morelos Reef National Park","Juan Escutia wreck dive","Route of the Cenotes Puerto Morelos","Puerto Morelos fishing village","Puerto Morelos vs Cancun value"],"search_language":"es-MX (restated, not machine-translated)","local_keywords":["arrecife Puerto Morelos","Parque Nacional Arrecife de Puerto Morelos","buceo pecio Juan Escutia","Ruta de los Cenotes","pueblo pesquero Puerto Morelos","villas frente al mar Puerto Morelos","qué hacer en Puerto Morelos"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04"},"booking":{"bin":"freely_bookable","level":"L2","codes":[],"consent_flow":false,"note":"Quintana Roo/Mexico US L2 (Exercise Increased Caution) - freely bookable; MXN currency, USD widely accepted"},"si_checklist_25":{"run_date":"2026-07-31","hits":7,"misses":15,"disregarded":3,"note":"Canonical 25-SI list; sports limited to participant; spectator/prosports/compsports disregarded"},"sis_present":[{"si":"diveglobal","name":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"ocean","name":"ocean","status":"future"},{"si":"globaladv","name":"adventure","status":"future"},{"si":"culinary","name":"culinary","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Zoëtry / Royalton Reserve Paraíso de la Bonita, a Luxury Collection Resort, Riviera Maya","why_ultra":"IN Puerto Morelos (Hwy Km 328); 90-100 ocean-front suites w/ plunge pools, 14 acres, thalasso spa, one of only 3 Luxury Collection all-inclusives worldwide, AAA Five Diamond 15 yrs (Zoëtry heritage); rebranded to Royalton Reserve adults-only, operating 2026 - verify current brand","earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso (Marriott Luxury Collection + Royalton/Blue Diamond); verify %","virtuoso_value_add":"verify Marriott STARS/Luxury Collection amenities - not documented","mor":"commission-on-net; no net-rate resale markup","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Hotel_Review-g240327-d28213141-Reviews-Royalton_Reserve_Paraiso_de_la_Bonita_a_Luxury_Collection_Resort_Riviera_Maya_Adult_A.html"},{"name":"Mayakoba enclave (Rosewood / Banyan Tree / Fairmont / Andaz) - ADJACENT, verify municipality","why_ultra":"620-acre gated ultra enclave, 4 flagship resorts; STRAIGHT GEOGRAPHY: administratively in Solidaridad (Km 298, Playa del Carmen area), NOT Puerto Morelos - do not label as in Puerto Morelos; nearest true-ultra cluster + standard corridor pull-out","earning":"on application / via host-Virtuoso (Rosewood Elite / Fairmont / Hyatt Prive / Banyan Tree); verify %","virtuoso_value_add":"Rosewood Mayakoba is Virtuoso-preferred - verify current amenity package","mor":"commission-on-net; no resale markup","source":"https://www.jetsetchristina.com/where-to-stay-in-mayakoba-mexico-rosewood-vs-fairmont-vs-andaz-vs-banyan-tree/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Puerto Morelos, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.8478,"lng":-86.8758}}'::jsonb, 27),
  ('roatan-honduras', '10S', 'Roatán, Honduras (Bay Islands)', 'Honduras', 'Roatán', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Honduras', '{"diveglobal","tropical"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Roatán sits on the Mesoamerican Barrier Reef, the second-largest coral-reef system on earth; Bay Islands ranked highest in coral health in the 2015 Mesoamerican assessment.","30+ dive shops on the west side; ~30 named dive sites within a 10-minute boat ride off West Bay/West End, with walls dropping past 100 ft and the El Aguila/Odyssey wrecks.","The Roatán Aggressor IV liveaboard runs Sat->Sat (18 guests, ~24-27 dives) across Roatán, Cayos Cochinos, and Utila.","Whale sharks are snorkel-only and protected; Utila (a short hop from Roatán) offers year-round potential peaking late March-April.","Roatán has an on-island recompression chamber (Cornerstone Hyperbaric, adjacent to Anthony''s Key Resort; DAN IPPN partner) — a first-response advantage for wall diving."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hyperbaric_chamber":"Cornerstone Hyperbaric Chamber & Clinic, Sandy Bay (adjacent to Anthony''s Key Resort) — on-island recompression chamber + ER/lab/pharmacy, DAN International Preferred Provider Network partner","book_enabled":true,"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","consent_flow":{"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live US State Dept advisory for Honduras (level + reason + named-danger areas + complete ''If you decide to travel'' guidance, pulled live), plus traveler acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only — final consent language PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"},"air_access_verified":"Direct air into Juan Manuel Gálvez Intl (RTB), Roatán — Bay Islands reachable without transiting mainland gang zones","no_fly_after_diving":"18-24 hours before RTB departure flight (DAN protocol)","environmental":["west-wall depth discipline","currents on walls/channels","dengue (CDC)","bottled water only"]},"timing":{"peak_season":"mid-December to April (dry season); whale-shark peak late March-April; secondary Oct-Dec","best_visibility":"July-September","curve_start":"late November (dry-season); early March (whale-shark spike)","inflection":"December peak; late-March-April whale-shark peak","fire_date":"early-to-mid November (dry-season peak); mid-February (whale-shark spike)","booking_lead_months":"4-6","off_season_fill":"September-November (rain / hurricane-fringe) — value window, visibility-driven dive messaging","dive_calendar":true},"jewels":[{"name":"West End Wall + Mary''s Place","si_tag":"diveglobal","tier":"premier","source":"https://sundiversroatan.com/roatan-diving/","hook":"West End Wall is a top-tier wall dive","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"West End Wall is a top-tier wall dive","commission":"dive-resort package (Fora) / own-CLIA liveaboard"},{"name":"Shark Dive — Cara a Cara (via Waihuka)","si_tag":"Diving/GEA","tier":"comfort","source":"https://roatan.online/cara-cara-shark-dive","hook":"face-to-face with 8–15 Caribbean reef sharks at ~70 ft; ~$120 pp + 15% tax","si":"Diving/GEA","blurb":"face-to-face with 8–15 Caribbean reef sharks at ~70 ft; ~$120 pp + 15% tax","commission":"excursion via DMC/dive-resort (Fora)"},{"name":"Cayos Cochinos","si_tag":"Diving/Liveaboard","tier":"premier","source":"https://divemagazine.com/scuba-diving-travel/americas-caribbean/aggressor-adventures-roatan-aggressor-liveaboard-highlights","hook":"protected archipelago of pristine, less-dived reefs — a Roatán Aggressor itinerary highlight","si":"Diving/Liveaboard","blurb":"protected archipelago of pristine, less-dived reefs — a Roatán Aggressor itinerary highlight","commission":"own-CLIA liveaboard"},{"name":"El Aguila & Odyssey wrecks","si_tag":"diveglobal","tier":"premier","source":"https://diveintolife.blog/scuba-diving-in-roatan-honduras-west-bay-west-end/","si":"diveglobal","commission":"dive-resort package (Fora)"},{"name":"Whale-shark snorkel (Utila day-trip)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.thisisutila.com/post/utila-s-whale-shark-season-when-to-come-and-what-to-expect","si":"expedition","commission":"day-trip excursion via DMC (Fora)"},{"name":"Dolphin Encounter (Anthony''s Key Resort)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://anthonyskey.com/dolphin-programs/","hook":"get-in-the-water dolphin program in a natural lagoon; a 50-year AKR institution","si":"expedition","blurb":"get-in-the-water dolphin program in a natural lagoon; a 50-year AKR institution","commission":"AKR package/excursion (Fora)"},{"name":"Gumbalimba Park (ziplines, capuchins, iguanas, macaws)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://roatan.online/gumbalimba-park","si":"expedition","commission":"DMC excursion (Fora/affiliate)"},{"name":"Iguana Farm (near French Cay, 2,700+ iguanas)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://roatantourbase.com/excursion-guides/our-favorite-things-to-do-and-see-in-coxen-hole","si":"expedition","commission":"DMC excursion (affiliate)"},{"name":"Punta Gorda — Garífuna culture (UNESCO)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://roatantourbase.com/excursion-guides/our-favorite-things-to-do-and-see-in-coxen-hole","hook":"Roatán''s oldest settlement; UNESCO-recognized Garífuna heritage, with the April 12 anniversary celebration","si":"expedition","blurb":"Roatán''s oldest settlement; UNESCO-recognized Garífuna heritage, with the April 12 anniversary celebration","commission":"cultural excursion via DMC (Fora/affiliate)"},{"name":"West Bay Beach","si_tag":"Tropical/Beaches","source":"https://www.royalcaribbean.com/inspire/what-is-roatan-known-for","hook":"Roatán''s iconic white-sand shoreline; warm shallows, reef snorkeling straight off the sand","si":"Tropical/Beaches","blurb":"Roatán''s iconic white-sand shoreline; warm shallows, reef snorkeling straight off the sand","commission":"anchors West Bay resort/villa stays (Fora / MoR villa)","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"The load-bearing risk is mainland crime, and the plan is to stay in-zone. Violent crime and gang activity concentrate in the San Pedro Sula, Tegucigalpa, and Comayagua corridors, and Gracias a Dios Department carries a Level 4 \"Do Not Travel\" rating — all on the mainland. Fly direct into RTB, keep the trip airport → island, and never route overland through the gang zones.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2024-12-10","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is diving Roatán''s walls dangerous — and can I fly out afterward?","a":"Wall diving rewards depth discipline and respect for the no-fly window, and Roatán has an unusual first-response advantage. Recreational divers work the crest and upper wall (≤60–100 ft); wreck and deep-wall profiles trend technical and are certification-gated. Allow no-fly-after-diving of 18–24 hours before your RTB flight, and note the on-island Cornerstone Hyperbaric Chamber (adjacent to Anthony''s Key Resort, a DAN partner) — a genuine safety edge for a wall-diving island. **What makes Roatán''s diving special? ** *(Dive Liveaboards / Diving)* Roatán delivers a serious wall reef within minutes of the dock plus a rare repeat-rate track record. Within a 10-minute boat ride off West Bay/West End you reach ~30 named dive sites, from a 15-ft sandy playground with feeding eagle rays to 100-ft+ wall drop-offs, wrecks, and canyon swim-throughs; CoCo View Resort claims the highest repeat rate of any dive resort worldwide (1,600+ guests five times over).","source":"anthonyskey.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"How much is the Roatán reef fee, and is it required?","a":"Yes, it is mandatory and it is small. The Roatán Marine Park conservation fee is $10/year or $5/day, non-commissionable, and it funds the very reef you came to dive and snorkel — present it as the reef''s cover charge, never buried.","source":"roatan.online, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Is Roatán good for a honeymoon?","a":"Yes — Roatán runs a genuine adults-only luxury lane on top of the diving. Ibagari Boutique Hotel is adults-only (12+), holds a Michelin Key 2025, and sits between West Bay and West End; private West Bay villas and sunset-cocktail liveaboard finales round out the romance product.","source":"guide.michelin.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can I snorkel with whale sharks from Roatán?","a":"Yes, via a day-trip to neighboring Utila, and only by snorkel. Utila is one of the few places on earth with year-round whale-shark potential, peaking late March–April; the animals are protected, so it is surface snorkeling only — no diving with them and no touching.","source":"thisisutila.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"adventure"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Roatán, Honduras (Bay Islands) — Diving, Liveaboards & West Bay Beach | TravelWell.World","search_language":"es-HN","local_keywords":["buceo Roatán","West Bay Roatán","Islas de la Bahía","tiburón ballena Utila","arrecife mesoamericano buceo","hoteles de buceo Roatán","cámara hiperbárica Roatán"],"long_tail_en":["Roatán diving guide","Roatán liveaboard Aggressor","West Bay Beach Roatán","whale shark snorkel Utila from Roatán","is Roatán safe to visit 2026","Roatán hyperbaric chamber"],"hreflang":["en","es-HN"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","primary_keyword":"Roatán"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"diveglobal","status":"live"},{"si":"tropical","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Ibagari Boutique Hotel","lane":"Fora / Virtuoso preferred","mor":"Fora","tier":"Ultra/Luxury","note":"adults-only, Michelin Key 2025, boutique dive center"},{"name":"Las Verandas Hotel & Villas (Pristine Bay)","lane":"Fora / Virtuoso","mor":"Fora","tier":"Luxury","note":"villa resort + Black Pearl golf"},{"name":"Turquoise Bay Dive & Beach Resort","lane":"Fora","mor":"Fora","tier":"premier","note":"remote NE all-inclusive dive"},{"name":"Private West Bay villas (Arca / Lighthouse Estates)","lane":"MoR villa rung","mor":"MoR","tier":"Luxury","note":"full-villa buyout + DMC concierge"},{"name":"Roatán Aggressor private charter","lane":"own-CLIA","mor":"CLIA","tier":"Ultra/Premium","note":"full 18-berth whole-boat buyout"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Roatán, Honduras (Bay Islands), Honduras"},"geo":{"lat":16.3,"lng":-86.53}}'::jsonb, 28),
  ('san-andres-colombia', '10S', 'San Andrés & Providencia, Colombia', 'Colombia', 'Coral islet, seven-colour sea', 'live', 'verified', 'tropicalBeach', 'Colombia''s Caribbean Coast', '{"tropical","liveaboard","romance","culture"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","premier","luxury"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["San Andrés — the ''Sea of Seven Colors'' — is Colombia''s Caribbean crown jewel, ringed by coral with 40+ mostly-shallow, high-visibility dive sites.","Providencia + Santa Catalina sit on the third-largest barrier reef in the world; Providencia rebuilt after Hurricane Iota (2020) and is open to tourism in 2026.","The Raizal are a Black Colombian Afro-Caribbean people; 20,000–30,000 speak San Andrés–Providencia Creole (Islander English) and most are trilingual.","Rondón — fish, conch, cassava, plantain and yam simmered in coconut milk — is the island''s signature dish (''run down'').","Mandatory Tourist Card (Tarjeta de Turismo) ~COP 153,000 (2026), bought at the airline counter before boarding the flight to ADZ."],"safety":{"emergency":"123","hospital":"Hospital Departamental Clarence Lynd Newball (San Andrés); hyperbaric/decompression chamber at Timothy Britton Hospital, San Andrés; serious cases referred off-island to mainland or US","book_enabled":true,"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","risk_codes":["C","T","U","K","N"],"risk_code_meanings":{"C":"Crime — violent crime (murder, assault, robbery), drugging (scopolamine/burundanga), extortion, express kidnapping occur throughout Colombia incl. cities (island crime skews to petty/beach theft + motorcycle snatch-and-grab)","T":"Terrorism — attacks possible with little/no warning; car bombs, grenades, IEDs, drones (mainland-weighted)","U":"Unrest — demonstrations can shut roads and turn violent","K":"Kidnapping or Hostage-Taking — kidnapping-for-ransom reported (mainland-weighted)","N":"Natural Disaster — mainland volcano/earthquake/landslide; archipelago hurricane/tropical-storm exposure (Hurricane Iota, Nov 2020)"},"named_danger":["Arauca","Cauca excl Popayán","Valle del Cauca excl Cali","Norte de Santander","Venezuela border ~10km"],"archipelago_in_named_danger":false,"island_crime_note":"island petty-crime (beach theft, motorcycle snatch-and-grab, scooter accidents) is lower and different from mainland violent crime; country-level advisory still renders in full at consent","consent_flow":{"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live US State Dept advisory for Colombia (level + reason + named-danger areas + complete ''If you decide to travel'' guidance, pulled live) + traveler acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only — final consent language PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"},"air_access_verified":"ADZ (Gustavo Rojas Pinilla Intl) — direct international from Panama City (Copa, year-round) + domestic Colombian hubs; no nonstop US, but 1-stop via BOG/PTY (Avianca, Copa, LATAM). Providencia reached by ~20-min inter-island flight or catamaran.","remote_flag":true,"water":"bottled","vaccinations":"dengue/chikungunya/Zika present (peak rainy months); use insect protection; check CDC","scopolamine_caution":"''devil''s breath''/burundanga drugging — country-level; concentrates on mainland; never accept drinks/food from strangers"},"timing":{"peak":"Dec–Apr (dry); true peak January, then Feb–Mar (Colombians'' favorite domestic island)","inflection_curve_start":"early December","fire_date":"mid-to-late November (Dec–Jan peak); ~4–6 weeks before Semana Santa (late-Feb/early-Mar) for the Easter spike","event_peaks":[{"event":"Christmas–New Year","dates":"Dec 20–31","note":"maximum annual congestion; ADZ seats + rooms sell out"},{"event":"Semana Santa (Holy Week)","dates_2026":"Mar/Apr","note":"intense domestic coastal surge"}],"off_season_fill":"Sep–Nov (green season, lowest crowds, best deals); Jul–Aug secondary dry spell = best weather-to-cost; note higher dengue in rainy months"},"jewels":[{"name":"Sea of Seven Colors (Spratt Bight + lagoon)","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","source":"https://colombia.travel/en/san-andres-island","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the seven-shade turquoise-to-cobalt water off the North End and the Aquarium/Haynes Cay flats; the island''s signature image","si":"tropical","blurb":"the seven-shade turquoise-to-cobalt water off the North End and the Aquarium/Haynes Cay flats; the island''s signature image","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"hotel + boat-tour affiliate"},{"name":"Johnny Cay","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/colombia/san-andres-and-providencia/san-andres/attractions/johnny-cay-natural-regional-park/","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"protected 4-ha coral islet ~1.5 km off San Andrés Town, coconut groves and the best white-sand beach around; colectivo boats from the town beach","si":"tropical","blurb":"protected 4-ha coral islet ~1.5 km off San Andrés Town, coconut groves and the best white-sand beach around; colectivo boats from the town beach","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"GetYourGuide/Viator day-trip affiliate + park entry (non-comm)"},{"name":"La Piscinita","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g3493965-d3228746-Reviews-La_Piscinita-San_Andres_San_Andres_Island_San_Andres_and_Providencia_Department.html","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"calm natural snorkel pool south of El Cove, dive board + water slide, reef fish, seafood restaurant + gear rental","si":"tropical","blurb":"calm natural snorkel pool south of El Cove, dive board + water slide, reef fish, seafood restaurant + gear rental","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"day-tour affiliate + on-site entry (non-comm)"},{"name":"West View (Mermaid Cave)","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","source":"https://travelhapp.com/inspiration/things-to-do-in-san-andres-and-providencia","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"tropical","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"day-tour affiliate + entry (non-comm)"},{"name":"Rocky Cay + San Luis beach","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","source":"https://colombia.travel/en/san-andres-island","hook":"walk-out cay off the quieter San Luis east coast, shallow wading to a wreck, the island''s mellow beach zone","si":"tropical","blurb":"walk-out cay off the quieter San Luis east coast, shallow wading to a wreck, the island''s mellow beach zone","commission":"San Luis hotel + day-tour affiliate"},{"name":"El Cove","si_tag":"tropical","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/colombia/san-andres-and-providencia/san-andres/attractions/la-piscinita/","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the island''s deepest natural anchorage on the West side, quiet local-life counterpoint to the North End","si":"tropical","blurb":"the island''s deepest natural anchorage on the West side, quiet local-life counterpoint to the North End","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"island-tour affiliate"},{"name":"Sea of Seven Colors reef dives + walls (Blue Wall, The Pyramid, Blue Diamond wreck)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards / Diving","tier":"essential","source":"https://bandadive.com/en","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"Dive Liveaboards / Diving","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"PADI operator direct/affiliate (Banda, Sharky)"},{"name":"Providencia barrier reef (third-largest on earth)","si_tag":"Dive Liveaboards / Diving","tier":"premier","source":"https://colombia.travel/en/providencia","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"wall and reef diving off Providencia/Santa Catalina, wilder and less-visited than San Andrés","si":"Dive Liveaboards / Diving","blurb":"wall and reef diving off Providencia/Santa Catalina, wilder and less-visited than San Andrés","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"Providencia dive operator direct + inter-island flight"},{"name":"Providencia + Crab Cay + McBean Lagoon","si_tag":"romance","tier":"premier","source":"https://cuppatocopatravels.com/south-america/colombia/guide-isla-de-providencia-colombia/","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the quiet-honeymoon jewel: Crab Cay ranked the island''s 1 snorkel spot, the McBean Lagoon marine park, near-empty coves","si":"romance","blurb":"the quiet-honeymoon jewel: Crab Cay ranked the island''s 1 snorkel spot, the McBean Lagoon marine park, near-empty coves","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"Providencia DMC/boutique + marine-park fee (non-comm)"},{"name":"San Luis sunset stays","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","source":"https://colombia.travel/en/san-andres-island/native-inns","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the mellow east-coast beach strip, sunset-side quiet, small hotels and native inns for a low-key honeymoon","si":"romance","blurb":"the mellow east-coast beach strip, sunset-side quiet, small hotels and native inns for a low-key honeymoon","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"San Luis hotel affiliate + host"},{"name":"Raizal culture + Islander Creole","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raizal","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"a living Afro-Caribbean nation: Creole English, Baptist chapels, kinship ties across the western Caribbean","si":"culture","blurb":"a living Afro-Caribbean nation: Creole English, Baptist chapels, kinship ties across the western Caribbean","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"cultural-tour affiliate + native-inn stay"},{"name":"Rondón + coconut cuisine","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://colombiaone.com/2025/09/02/colombia-food-san-andres/","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the \"run down\" seafood-in-coconut-milk stew, breadfruit, crab, conch; a Raizal food-and-culture experience","si":"culture","blurb":"the \"run down\" seafood-in-coconut-milk stew, breadfruit, crab, conch; a Raizal food-and-culture experience","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"food-tour affiliate + restaurant"},{"name":"Morgan''s Cave","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://colombiaone.com/2023/12/21/guide-visit-san-andres-island-colombia/","timing":"Dec–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"legendary Henry Morgan pirate-treasure hideout, now a small theme park/museum with exhibits and dance shows","si":"culture","blurb":"legendary Henry Morgan pirate-treasure hideout, now a small theme park/museum with exhibits and dance shows","when":"Dec–Apr","commission":"island-tour affiliate + entry (non-comm)"}],"faq":[{"q":"What are the best beaches and cays on San Andrés?","a":"Johnny Cay is the headline — a protected 4-ha coral islet ~1.5 km off San Andrés Town with the best white sand around, reached by colectivo boat — plus calm snorkel pools at La Piscinita and West View, and mellow Rocky Cay off San Luis. The lagoon is the famed \"Sea of Seven Colors.\"","source":"lonelyplanet.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"Is San Andrés good for scuba diving?","a":"Yes — it''s a shallow-water reef diver''s dream, with 40+ dive sites mostly at ~10–12 m, high-visibility and beginner-friendly, run through island PADI centers like Banda and Sharky. Providencia adds wall diving on the third-largest barrier reef in the world. Note it''s day-boat reef diving, not liveaboard-berth product.","source":"divescover.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"Is Providencia good for a quiet honeymoon?","a":"Yes — Providencia is the quiet-honeymoon jewel: near-empty coves, the McBean Lagoon marine park, and Crab Cay (its #1 snorkel spot, ~USD $6 park fee) reached by express boat. It''s rebuilt and open after Hurricane Iota (2020); reach it by ~20-minute inter-island flight or catamaran.","source":"cuppatocopatravels.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What language and culture will I find on San Andrés?","a":"A living Raizal Afro-Caribbean nation: 20,000–30,000 people speak San Andrés–Providencia Creole (Islander English) and most are trilingual, descended from 18th-century Jamaican settlers and enslaved Africans. The signature plate is rondón — fish, conch and root vegetables simmered in coconut milk.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What''s the real day-to-day risk on the island?","a":"Not the mainland headlines — the island''s real risks are petty/beach theft, motorcycle snatch-and-grab, scooter accidents and sea/riptide hazards. Renting a scooter or golf cart is the classic island loop, and scooter crashes plus snatch-and-grab are the two most common tourist mishaps: helmet on, valuables off the seat, drive in daylight.","source":"travelsafe-abroad.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"San Andrés & Providencia, Colombia — Sea of Seven Colors Diving, Beaches & Raizal Culture | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-CO","long_tail_en":["things to do in San Andres Colombia","San Andres diving Sea of Seven Colors","is San Andres safe 2026","Providencia island Colombia guide","San Andres tourist card cost 2026","Johnny Cay day trip San Andres","Providencia Crab Cay snorkeling"],"local_keywords":["San Andrés qué hacer","buceo San Andrés","Providencia","tarjeta de turismo San Andrés","Johnny Cay San Andrés","Cueva de Morgan","rondón San Andrés"],"hreflang":["en","es-CO"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["tropical","Dive Liveaboards / Diving","romance","culture"],"ultra":[{"name":"Casa Harb","type":"design boutique — island top-end (luxury, NOT palace-ultra)","routing":"Fora/Virtuoso preferred where participating + host","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Decameron cluster (Isleño/San Luis/Los Delfines/Aquarium)","type":"mass-market all-inclusive","routing":"Online-Agency (OA) lane + host","tier":"premium (mass AI)"},{"name":"GHL Sunrise Hotel (Sunrise Beach)","type":"mid-market beachfront workhorse, Spratt Bight","routing":"GDS/bedbank + host","tier":"premier"},{"name":"Casa Iguana del Mar (villa)","type":"award-winning design villa, reef + white sand","routing":"MoR villa + host","tier":"luxury (thin)"},{"name":"Deep Blue (Providencia)","type":"boutique standout, Crab Cay gateway","routing":"direct/host","tier":"premium (remote boutique)"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"San Andrés & Providencia, Colombia, Colombia"},"geo":{"lat":12.5847,"lng":-81.7006}}'::jsonb, 29),
  ('tulum-mexico', '10S', 'Tulum', 'Mexico', 'Cliff-top Maya ruins and cenote diving', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Quintana Roo (Cancún & Riviera Maya)', '{"expedition","diveglobal","culture","wildlife"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Tulum ruins are the only Maya walled city built on a seaside cliff (El Castillo, Temple of the Frescoes).","Tulum sits above Sistema Sac Actun, a ~347 km interconnected underwater cave system.","Archaeological zone: 8am-5pm, last entry 3:30pm; best 8-10am.","Sian Ka''an Biosphere Reserve (UNESCO) borders the destination to the south.","Tulum''s open Atlantic-facing beaches are the worst-hit by sargassum in the Riviera Maya."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Nearest trauma: Hospiten Riviera Maya, Playa del Carmen (+52 984 159 2200), ~60 km north; local clinics stabilize/transfer; major trauma to Cancún","advisory_level":"L2","malaria":"none in tourist Quintana Roo","yellow_fever":"none required","fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel State of Baja California FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua State of Sinaloa FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route State of Tamaulipas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed by federal toll road 85D from Monterrey federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways State of Zacatecas FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro Federal Highway 15D State of Jalisco FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border with the state of Colima."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero State of Colima FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or air via the Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Guerrero, except the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to within 40km of the Guatemalan border between the Pacific Coast up to and including the border crossing at Gracias a Dio."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel on Federal Highway 199 (Carretera Federal 199) between Rancho Nuevo (just outside San Cristobal de las Casas) and the Chancalá junction just outside Palenque (where Federal Highway 199 meets Federal Highway 307)."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Acapulco."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tijuana, except: airside transit through Tijuana airport the Cross Border Xpress bridge from the airport linking terminals across the Mexican-US border the federal toll road 1D and Via Rápida through Tijuana to the border FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the city of Tecate in Baja California, including roads between Tijuana and Tecate."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Chihuahua, except: the city of Chihuahua the border crossing in Ciudad Juárez (accessed by federal toll road 45) federal toll road 45D connecting the cities of Chihuahua and Ciudad Juárez the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Chihuahua and towns immediately on this route including Creel the road from Creel via San Juanito to San Pedro state highway 16 from San Pedro to Chihuahua There are high levels of organised crime activity, particularly human and drugs trafficking."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Sinaloa, except: the cities of Los Mochis and Mazatlán road 32 that runs between El Fuerte and Los Mochis the 15D federal toll road that runs the length of the state the Copper Canyon rail route to and from Los Mochis, El Fuerte and the towns immediately on this route Armed robbery and vehicle theft has happened in El Fuerte."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Tamaulipas, except: the border crossing at Nuevo Laredo accessed from Monterrey by federal toll road 85D – you should travel during daylight hours federal highways 80, 81 and 85 between Tampico, Ciudad de Victoria and Magueyes, and the entire area of Tamaulipas south of these highways Tamaulipas is dangerous due to the presence of many organised crime groups who fight for control of drug trafficking routes."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Zacatecas."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of the road 45D."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the state of Michoacán, except the: city of Morelia accessed by federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43; and the federal toll road 48D between the city of Morelia and the General Francisco Mujica airport town of Pátzcuaro accessed by federal toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips out to islands on Lake Pátzcuaro federal highway 15D Michoacán is one of Mexico’s most violent states with high levels of organised crime and very little security presence."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the border state of Colima, specifically the municipalities of: Acatlán de Juárez Amacueca Ameca Atemajac de Brizuela Atengo Atenguillo Atoyac Autlán de Navarro Ayutla Casimiro Castillo Chiquilistlán Cocula Cuautitlán de García Barragán Cuautla Ejutla El Grullo El Limón Gómez Farias Guachinango Juchitlán Mixtlán San Gabriel San Marcos San Martín Hidalgo Sayula Tapalpa Techaluta de Montenegro Tecolotlán Tenamaxtlán Teocuitatlán de Corona Tolimán Tonaya Tuxcacuesco Tuxcueca Unión de Tula Villa Corona Villa Purificación Zacoalco de Torres Zapotitlán de Vadill Zapotlán el Grande FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the northern municipalities of: Bolaños Chimaltitán Colotlán Hostotipaquillo Huejúcar Huequilla el Alto Mezquitic San Martin de Bolaños Santa Maria de los Ángeles Totatiche Villa Guerrero This is due to inaccessibility for security forces, lack of state control, drugs cultivation and high levels of violence between rival criminal groups."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the whole state of Colima, except the city of Manzanillo accessed by sea or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport, and direct travel via road 200 from the airport to Manzanillo."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-16T16:08:09+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":"Nov-Apr (dry season)","shoulder":"Nov & Feb (best value inside peak)","green":"Apr-Oct (heat, hurricane Jun-Nov, sargassum Apr-Aug)","price_swing_peak_pct":"40-60% above shoulder","shoulder_discount_pct":"15-25% below peak","booking_lead":{"christmas_nye":"reserve by September (Dec 20-Jan 5 fully books; NYE is the flagship premium window)","feb_mar_peak":"book by November (incl. Spring Break + Holy Week 2026 Mar 29-Apr 5)"},"holiday_event_peaks":["New Year''s Eve","Christmas week","Holy Week 2026-03-29/2026-04-05","Spring Break (March)"],"out_of_season_fill":"Apr-Oct: sell ruins/cenotes/Sian Ka''an, not a beach promise; cenote diving is weather-independent + sargassum-immune","campaign_start_trigger":"NYE/Christmas by mid-August; Feb-Mar peak by early October; Apr-Aug campaigns must not promise pristine beach (sargassum guardrail)","source":"https://casatira.com/best-time-to-visit-tulum-month-by-month-weather-crowd-guide-for-2026"},"jewels":[{"name":"Dos Ojos cavern dive (Sistema Sac Actun)","si_tag":"Dive Globally","status":"future","hook":"Guided cavern dives with cathedral light in the world''s longest cave system.","bookable_category":"cenote cave/cavern dive (guide required)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/things-to-do-in-tulum/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"diveglobal","blurb":"Guided cavern dives with cathedral light in the world''s longest cave system.","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"Amstar 12% / affiliate 4-8%"},{"name":"Gran Cenote snorkel/intro dive","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Crystal-clear cenote with turtles and stalactites, all ages and levels.","bookable_category":"cenote tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/things-to-do-in-tulum/","si":"expedition","blurb":"Crystal-clear cenote with turtles and stalactites, all ages and levels.","commission":"Amstar 12%; entry pass-through"},{"name":"Tulum ruins at opening light","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Cliff-top Maya walled city with sea views no other Maya site can match.","bookable_category":"guided cultural excursion","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/tulum-ruins-guide/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"Cliff-top Maya walled city with sea views no other Maya site can match.","when":"year-round","commission":"Amstar 12%; ruin entry pass-through"},{"name":"Cobá jungle pyramids","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Taller jungle-clad Maya pyramids explorable by bike, ~28 mi north.","bookable_category":"guided cultural excursion","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/things-to-do-in-tulum/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"Taller jungle-clad Maya pyramids explorable by bike, ~28 mi north.","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"Amstar 12% / affiliate"},{"name":"Sian Ka''an Biosphere Reserve","si_tag":"Wildlife & Nature","status":"future","hook":"UNESCO biosphere lagoon float — an eco-safari and a sargassum-proof day.","bookable_category":"eco-tour","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/things-to-do-in-tulum/","timing":"Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"wildlife","blurb":"UNESCO biosphere lagoon float — an eco-safari and a sargassum-proof day.","when":"Nov-Apr","commission":"affiliate 4-8% / DMC 12%; biosphere fee pass-through"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Tulum?","a":"Sargassum above all — Tulum is the worst-hit beach stretch on the Riviera Maya, and 2026 is a record year, so beach quality is genuinely not guaranteed. Anchor the trip on ruins, cenotes and Sian Ka''an rather than a pristine-beach promise. Also plan for hurricane season (Jun–Nov), bottled water, and dengue (peak May–Nov, no malaria).","source":"deeparrival.com / cdc.gov, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is cenote and cave diving in Tulum dangerous?","a":"It demands the right certification for serious overhead-environment diving. Sistema Sac Actun and Dos Ojos are caves: cavern diving requires a certified cave/cavern guide and must stay in the daylight zone, and the dark cave zone requires full cave certification — no exceptions, no solo penetration. Observe no-fly of 18h single / 24h repetitive; the nearest chamber is ~60 km north.","source":"sssnetwork.com / mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"When should I visit the Tulum ruins?","a":"Right at the 8am opening. The archaeological zone runs 8am–5pm (last entry 3:30pm), and the 8–10am window beats both the heat and the crowds at this cliff-top walled city. Come in November or February for low crowds and ideal temperatures; Holy Week (2026: Mar 29–Apr 5) runs at full capacity and Apr–Oct heat is intense.","source":"absolute-adventure-mexico.com / mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What are the best cenotes for diving near Tulum?","a":"Gran Cenote and Dos Ojos lead — Tulum sits above Sistema Sac Actun, a ~347 km interconnected cave system, the densest cenote country in Mexico. Gran Cenote (2.5 mi from town) is an all-levels swim/snorkel/intro-dive; Dos Ojos is the marquee guided cavern dive. All are weather-independent and sargassum-immune, making them the reliable core of a Tulum trip.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"diveglobal"},{"q":"Will sargassum ruin the Tulum beaches in 2026?","a":"Be realistic: Tulum is the worst-hit stretch on the coast, its open Atlantic-facing beaches catch the full brunt, and 2026 is a record/near-record year — beach quality is not guaranteed. Don''t cancel; re-anchor. Build the trip on ruins, cenotes and the Sian Ka''an biosphere (all sargassum-proof), and for reliable sand, the Punta Maroma stretch ~1 hour north sits north of the worst.","source":"deeparrival.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"tropical"},{"q":"What is Tulum''s wellness scene like?","a":"It is Tulum''s defining draw — yoga, temazcal ceremonies, cenote healing and jungle spas concentrated along the beach road. A signature is a north-Tulum cove with a beachfront cenote where you swim fresh and salt water in one spot, paired with jungle wellness. Book through a boutique hotel or DMC; some of the best programs are direct-only.","source":"mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"wellness"},{"q":"Is Tulum good for a honeymoon, and where''s the luxury?","a":"Yes — it is a honeymoon icon, built on bohemian-luxe boutiques and staffed villas. On the beach road, design icons like Azulik and Our Habitas Tulum lead (many are direct-only — verify the channel); for branded ultra beyond the sargassum, Maroma (A Belmond Hotel) and the 70-villa Chablé Maroma sit ~1 hour north. Fully staffed beach villas are the top private rung.","source":"virtuoso.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Tulum, and how far ahead do I book?","a":"November–April is the dry high season; November and February are the best value inside it (roughly 15–25% below peak), with November the single best month (dry, minimal seaweed, pre-holiday prices). Peak weeks run 40–60% above shoulder — reserve Christmas/NYE by September and Feb–March by November, as the boutique scene sells out months ahead.","source":"casatira.com / boldlygo.world, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"planning"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Tulum Travel Guide 2026 — Maya Ruins, Cenotes, Sian Ka''an & Straight Sargassum | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Plan Tulum: cliff-top Maya ruins at dawn, Sistema Sac Actun cenote diving, Sian Ka''an biosphere, plus straight 2026 sargassum reality, Level 2 safety and dive-chamber contacts.","slug":"tulum-mexico","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-04","search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["ruinas de Tulum horarios","mejor época para visitar Tulum","cenotes Tulum buceo","sargazo Tulum 2026","Sian Ka''an tour","villas de lujo Tulum","hoteles boutique Tulum"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"diveglobal","status":"future"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"wildlife","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Maroma, A Belmond Hotel","what":"Iconic Punta Maroma beach resort, reimagined 2023, ~1h north of Tulum","why_ultra":"Belmond/LVMH flag, best regional beach north of Tulum sargassum zone","earning":"agent/consortium — on application via host-Virtuoso","virtuoso":"Virtuoso-listed (upgrade, breakfast, ~$100-200 credit, early/late)","mor":"consortium-rack — safe (green)","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.virtuoso.com/travel/luxury-hotels/6163634/maroma-a-belmond-hotel-riviera-maya"},{"name":"Chablé Maroma","what":"70 pool-villa wellness retreat on Punta Maroma, cenote spa","why_ultra":"Destination-spa ultra, private-pool villas","earning":"agent/consortium — on application via host-Virtuoso","virtuoso":"Virtuoso-listed (VIP amenities)","mor":"consortium-rack — safe (green)","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.virtuoso.com/travel/luxury-hotels/15885219/chable-maroma"},{"name":"Azulik Tulum","what":"Adults-only treehouse eco villas, candlelit, cenote-fed baths, Tulum beach road","why_ultra":"Singular design icon, definitive Tulum eco-ultra (polarizing)","earning":"verify — largely direct-only; on application","virtuoso":"not confirmed — treat as direct-only, flag","mor":"amber — confirm booking channel before quoting commission","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://travel.usnews.com/hotels/review-azulik_-_adults_eco-resort_maya_spa-tulum-mexico-27488/"},{"name":"Casa Malca","what":"Former Pablo Escobar beachfront mansion, art-filled boutique hotel, Tulum beach road","why_ultra":"One-of-one provenance + curated art; boutique-ultra scarcity","earning":"on application — many beach-road boutiques direct-only; verify channel","virtuoso":"verify listing","mor":"amber — direct-only risk, confirm before net-rate","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://casamalca.com/"},{"name":"Our Habitas Tulum","what":"Adults-only canvas-and-wood beachfront eco sanctuary, quiet Tulum beach road, reef-regeneration program","why_ultra":"Design-forward luxe-eco with strong wellness/community program","earning":"on application via host / brand TA program","virtuoso":"on Visa Signature / Mr & Mrs Smith — verify Virtuoso","mor":"confirm channel — amber","price_tier":"luxury-ultra","source":"https://www.ourhabitas.com/tulum/"},{"name":"Staffed ultra villas — Tulum beach road","what":"Fully-staffed multi-bedroom beachfront villas (e.g. 10-BR Villa Privada), chef + concierge","why_ultra":"Buy-out privacy, staffed service, direct beach access — top villa rung","earning":"commissionable via villa specialist (VOD / Journey Mexico / Isle Blue / Loco Luxury)","virtuoso":"via villa-consortium programs","mor":"commissionable-rack = safe (green); net-rate resale = flag red","price_tier":"ultra","source":"https://www.loco.luxury/villaprivada"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-04","hero":{"query":"Tulum, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.2114,"lng":-87.4654}}'::jsonb, 30),
  ('utila-honduras', '10S', 'Utila', 'Honduras', 'Utila Honduras diving', 'live', 'verified', 'oceanAerial', 'Honduras', '{"liveaboard","tropical","expedition"}', '{"tropical"}', '{"essential","comfort"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["World''s cheapest PADI/SSI Open Water cert (~US$280-350), free/discounted dorm while diving; 60+ dive sites on the Mesoamerican Barrier Reef (2nd-largest on Earth)","Whale sharks year-round (best Mar-May + Aug-Sep); snorkel-only from the surface - scuba diving WITH whale sharks is prohibited","Reached by air to Roatan (RTB) or San Pedro Sula (SAP) + ferry from La Ceiba (~1 hr, ~US$35, Utila Dream ferry - sole operator); Utila airstrip is private-charter only","Budget-to-boutique dive island; ceiling = dive-resort lodge (Utila Lodge 8 over-water rooms, Mango Inn); NO branded ultra on-island - Roatan/Guanaja hold the luxury tier","The Cays / Water Cay uninhabited white-sand sandbar (Sun Jam festival site); Utila Cays Garifuna fishing village (Jewel + Pigeon/Suc-Suc); Chepes Beach; endangered Utila spiny-tailed iguana station"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (national police/fire/ambulance, Honduras - verify locally)","hyperbaric_chamber":"ON-ISLAND - Utila has its own chamber (at Utila Lodge, also doubling as island trauma center; a chamber also via Bay Islands College of Diving/College of Diving); a genuine asset most small dive islands lack","no_fly_after_diving":true,"hospital":"small clinics only + the Utila Lodge hyperbaric/trauma center on-island; serious trauma/complex dive cases route OFF-ISLAND to La Ceiba (mainland) then mainland hospital or US medevac; carry travel-medical + air-evac + DAN dive insurance","remote_flag":true,"book_enabled":true,"l3_disclosure":true,"consent_flow":{"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live US State Dept advisory for Honduras (level + reason + named-danger areas incl. Gracias a Dios L4 + the complete ''If you decide to travel'' guidance, pulled live) plus traveler acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only — PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"},"state_dept_carveout":"Bay Islands (Roatan/Utila/Guanaja) explicitly noted by State as better-policed resource-concentration areas; Gracias a Dios Dept = Level 4 Do Not Travel (isolated eastern mainland); danger is mainland, away from Utila","stay_in_zone":true,"air_access_verified":"RTB (Roatan) or SAP (San Pedro Sula) international arrival, then ferry to Utila from La Ceiba (~1 hr, ~US$35, Utila Dream ferry) or Roatan-Utila ferry; Utila airstrip = private charter only; routing never touches mainland gang zones","founder_policy_note":"book_enabled rides on the BOOK WITH WARNING bin (Four-Bin v3): full verbatim live US State Dept advisory disclosed + acknowledged at booking; named danger is mainland (Gracias a Dios L4 + urban gang zones), Bay Islands carved out; keep client in-zone","reef_safety":"protected Mesoamerican marine reserve - no-touch/no-stand, reef-safe sunscreen; wall/deep-site currents; whale-shark no-touch/no-scuba boat protocol","dengue":"dengue occasionally reported on Utila - protect against daytime Aedes (DEET/picaridin)","sandfly":"sandflies/no-see-ums are the signature nuisance, most active dusk-to-dawn; standard DEET underperforms - use oil-based lotion (Skin So Soft), cover up, net/fan at night; bites rarely carry leishmaniasis","water":"tap water NOT potable - bottled/refill only; mind ice/raw produce; wash hands before eating"},"timing":{"peak":"Dec-Apr (dry season; Christmas-New Year + Easter/Semana Santa sub-peaks)","whale_shark_subpeaks":"Mar-May and Aug-Sep (year-round presence; best odds; Aug-Sep is a green-season demand spike)","shoulder_green":"late-Oct-mid/late-Feb rains + Sep-Oct highest storm risk (value trough; but Sep is a whale-shark sub-peak); value island stays busy with cert traffic","booking_window_lead_time":"TWO SPEEDS - dive-cert/backpacker = short-lead (days-to-weeks, walk-in dorms, rolling last-minute layer); over-water dive-lodge tier + peak whale-shark weeks + Christmas/Easter = 2-4 months ahead","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"dive-cert value packages, Aug-Sep whale-shark spike at shoulder rates, freediving courses (weather-resilient), new-moon night dives, Cays day-trips between storms","holiday_event_peaks":"Christmas-New Year, Easter/Semana Santa, Sun Jam (Water Cay, ~August - verify dates), whale-shark sub-peaks as de-facto events","fire_date":"dry-peak: early-to-mid November (curve-start late-Nov minus 1-2 wks); Mar-May whale-shark: mid-February; Aug-Sep whale-shark: mid-July; dive-cert stays book-short-lead with permanent rolling last-minute layer","flag":"whale-shark sightings are probabilistic - market ''best odds'' never a guarantee; sharpen dates on live booking-pace tracking","dive_calendar":true,"sources":["https://www.utilalodge.com/whale-shark-encounters","https://www.islaguru.com/articles/utila-travel-practical-guide","https://www.mango-inn.com/","https://www.freediveutila.com/"]},"jewels":[{"si_tag":"liveaboard","name":"PADI/SSI Open Water certification (world''s cheapest)","why":"~US$280-350, free dorm while diving; the entry drug that turns a 3-day stop into a 3-week stay","timing":"Dec-Apr","tier":"essential","source":"https://utiladivecenter.com/","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"dive-operator commission on application; CLIA dive-lane convert to commissioned agent"},{"si_tag":"liveaboard","name":"Night dive - ''string of pearls'' bioluminescence (Ted''s Point / Ron''s Wreck)","why":"kill the lights on a new moon and watch ostracod bioluminescence flash through the water column; hunting octopus","timing":"Dec-Apr","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.dive-utila.com/advanced-open-water-diver","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"dive-operator + CLIA lane"},{"si_tag":"liveaboard","name":"Halliburton wreck + Airport Caves (deep/wall)","why":"upright cargo-ship wreck ~30 m + cavern swim-throughs full of glassy sweepers - the reef''s set-pieces","timing":"Dec-Apr","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.dive-utila.com/advanced-open-water-diver","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"liveaboard","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"dive-operator + CLIA lane"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Whale-shark snorkel expedition","why":"snorkel beside the largest fish in the ocean, year-round; captains hunt the bait-ball boil + diving birds","timing":"year-round; peak odds Mar-May + Aug-Sep","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.utilalodge.com/whale-shark-encounters","si":"expedition","when":"year-round; peak odds Mar-May + Aug-Sep","commission":"operator/expedition commission on application + Viator/GYG affiliate; CLIA-lane crossover"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Freediving course (Freedive Utila - Central America''s freediving HQ)","why":"learn to fall through the blue on one breath at the region''s only competitive freediving cooperative","timing":"Dec-Apr","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.freediveutila.com/","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"course commission on application"},{"si_tag":"expedition","name":"Utila Iguana Station (endangered spiny-tailed ''swamper'' iguana)","why":"conservation center for the iguana found only on Utila, living in its mangroves - a meaningful low-cost morning","timing":"Dec-Apr","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.islaguru.com/articles/things-to-do-utila-island-honduras","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"non-commissionable conservation donation - value-add/character stop, not a margin line"},{"si_tag":"tropical","name":"Water Cay (the Cays) day-trip","why":"tiny uninhabited white-sand island + sandbar ringed by coral; snorkel-and-sandbar paradise; Sun Jam festival site","timing":"year-round, calm-day best; festival ~August","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.utilawatersport.com/water-cay","si":"tropical","when":"year-round, calm-day best; festival ~August","commission":"local boat/tour operator + Viator affiliate (marine-park fee non-commissionable)"},{"si_tag":"tropical","name":"Utila Cays - Jewel Cay & Pigeon (Suc-Suc) Garifuna fishing village","why":"two cays joined by a footbridge, ~500 people on stilt homes over the water - a Garifuna/Caymanian fishing-village time capsule","timing":"Dec-Apr","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.utilaguide.com/activities/cays/","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"tropical","when":"Dec-Apr","commission":"local boat operator + F&B affiliate-adjacent"},{"si_tag":"tropical","name":"Chepes Beach + Rehab bar","why":"the island''s largest public beach - soft white sand, shallow calm water, beachfront bar; the free between-dives afternoon","timing":"year-round","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.islaguru.com/articles/things-to-do-utila-island-honduras","si":"tropical","when":"year-round","commission":"F&B/OTA-adjacent scene-setter, not a margin line"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Two risks are load-bearing: mainland crime and island remoteness. The advisory names Gracias a Dios Department (Level 4 \"Do Not Travel\") and urban mainland gang zones — all away from Utila, so keep the client in-zone (airport → ferry/charter → island). Separately, serious trauma or complex dive injuries route off-island to La Ceiba then a mainland hospital or US medevac, so carry travel-medical, air-evac, and DAN dive insurance without exception.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2024-12-10","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is learning to dive here dangerous, and can I fly out afterward?","a":"Diving here rewards a certified operator and disciplined profiles, and Utila has an unusual on-island safety asset. Certify only with a PADI/SSI-certified shop (UDC, Alton''s, Parrots, College of Diving, Underwater Vision), dive within no-decompression limits, and observe no-fly-after-diving of 18–24 hours before flying. Utila has its own hyperbaric chamber at Utila Lodge (doubling as the island trauma center), with a chamber also via Bay Islands College of Diving — a genuine asset most small dive islands lack.","source":"utilalodge.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Why is Utila the cheapest place to learn to dive?","a":"Utila built its name as the place backpackers came to get certified for a few hundred dollars and never left. A PADI/SSI Open Water course runs roughly US$280–350 — among the cheapest on Earth — with free or discounted dorm accommodation while you dive, on a reef with 60+ dive sites a few fin-kicks off the dock.","source":"alongdustyroads.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"liveaboard"},{"q":"Can I dive with the whale sharks, or only snorkel?","a":"Snorkel only — scuba diving with whale sharks is prohibited. As a protected species they are approached from the surface during surface intervals: captains hunt the \"boil/roil\" of feeding fish and diving birds, and you drop off the boat and snorkel beside them. Sightings are probabilistic (best odds Mar–May and Aug–Sep) — market \"best odds,\" never a guarantee.","source":"utilalodge.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What is there to do on Utila besides diving?","a":"Plenty above the water, all budget-friendly. Take a boat to Water Cay''s uninhabited white-sand sandbar, cold cans at Chepes Beach (the island''s largest public beach), the Utila Cays Garífuna fishing village of Jewel Cay and Pigeon (~500 people on stilt homes over the water), and Freedive Utila — Central America''s first freediving training center — where you learn to fall through the blue on one breath.","source":"islaguru.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"tropical"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Utila Honduras: Cheapest Dive Certs + Whale Sharks Year-Round","meta_description":"Get PADI-certified for ~$300, snorkel with year-round whale sharks, and explore Water Cay and the Mesoamerican reef — Utila is Honduras''s budget-to-boutique dive island. When to go, how to get there, and how to stay safe.","slug":"utila-honduras","primary_keyword":"Utila Honduras diving","long_tail":["cheapest PADI certification Utila","whale sharks Utila snorkel season","how to get to Utila from Roatan La Ceiba ferry","Utila vs Roatan diving budget","Water Cay Utila day trip","Freedive Utila freediving course","Utila hyperbaric chamber dive safety"],"search_language":"es-HN","local_keywords":["buceo Utila","tiburón ballena Utila","curso de buceo Utila","certificación PADI Utila barato","cómo llegar a Utila desde La Ceiba","Cayos de Utila / Water Cay","apnea Utila (freediving)"],"hreflang":["en","es-HN"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"liveaboard","status":"live"},{"si":"tropical","status":"live"},{"si":"expedition","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Private dive charter / private liveaboard day (out of Utila)","location":"on-Utila waters","posture":"the on-island ultra move is exclusivity on the water, not a hotel - private boat/guide/whale-shark hunt","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"local operator + David''s CLIA dive lane - convert to commissioned agent where offered","mor":"commissionable only where offered; no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.utilalodge.com/"},{"name":"Roatan luxury base (branded/boutique + dive-luxury lodges)","location":"neighboring Bay Island (short ferry/flight)","posture":"the Bay Islands'' actual luxury tier - route ultra client to a Roatan base, day/overnight to Utila for whale sharks","price_tier":"ultra/luxury","earning":"Fora / host-Virtuoso lane - commission on application","mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/traveladvisories/traveladvisories/honduras-travel-advisory.html"},{"name":"Guanaja private-island seclusion","location":"third/quietest Bay Island","posture":"small exclusive private-island/eco-luxury lodges - the no-crowds seclusion play","price_tier":"ultra","earning":"Fora / host-Virtuoso / CLIA - on application","mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.utilaguide.com/general/utilafaqs/"},{"name":"Utila on-island lodging","posture":"STATED PLAINLY: NO branded ultra on Utila; ceiling = comfortable dive-resort lodge (Utila Lodge / Mango Inn); sell as the whale-shark + dive day to a Roatan/Guanaja ultra base or a private charter","price_tier":"premier (ceiling)","earning":"n/a for ultra","mor":"no net-rate resale","source":"https://www.utilalodge.com/"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-07","hero":{"query":"Utila, Honduras"},"geo":{"lat":16.0983,"lng":-86.935}}'::jsonb, 31),
  ('antigua-guatemala', '10S', 'Antigua', 'Guatemala', 'Colonial streets under two volcanoes', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Guatemala', '{"expedition","culture","culinary","wildlife"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["UNESCO World Heritage colonial city (16th-18th c. Spanish architecture) cradled beneath Volcanoes Agua, Fuego and Acatenango.","Base for the Acatenango overnight trek (summit 3,976 m) with front-row views of continuously erupting Fuego; Pacaya (2,552 m) is the gentler guided lava hike.","Semana Santa is the most famous Holy Week in the Americas - dawn processions over colored-sawdust alfombras; books ~1 year ahead on tiny inventory.","Premier coffee origin: Finca Filadelfia (est. 1870) and nonprofit De la Gente run finca-to-cup tours minutes from the plaza.","A rising colonial-wedding and honeymoon destination anchored by converted-palace boutique hotels (Casa Santo Domingo, Palacio de Dona Leonor, Pensativo House)."],"safety":{"emergency":"110 police (PNC) / 122-123 bomberos (fire-rescue) / 128 Cruz Roja ambulance / 1500 PROATUR tourist assistance; Antigua POLITUR tourist police","hospital":"Hospital Nacional Pedro de Bethancourt (Antigua) + private clinics for stabilization; major trauma/evac to Guatemala City ~1 hr","book_enabled":true,"l3_disclosure":true,"state_dept_carveout":"Antigua/Sacatepequez explicitly cleared; avoid San Marcos/Huehuetenango/Zone-18/Villa Nueva","stay_in_zone":true,"air_access_verified":true,"altitude":"Antigua ~1,500 m (mild); Acatenango summit 3,976 m = serious AMS; Pacaya ~2,552 m","water":"bottled/purified only","malaria":"no malaria risk in Antigua (highland); dengue/Zika precaution advised","consent_flow":{"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live US State Dept advisory for the country (level + reason + named-danger areas + complete ''If you decide to travel'' guidance), pulled live, plus traveler acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only — final consent language PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"}},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"peak dry season Nov-Mar (baseline); Feb is the sweet spot (crowds dip, dry)","peak":"Semana Santa (Holy Week) late Mar/early Apr - THE event; 2027 ~Mar 24-28 (Good Friday Mar 26)","fire_date":"general dry-season curve: fire ~mid-October (curve-start -1-2 wks); Semana Santa 2027: fire ~Apr-May 2026 (~1 yr ahead), last-call ''book by January''","shoulder":"late Oct-Nov & Feb (dry, thinner crowds, easier rates)","green":"May-Oct wet season (lower rates; Sep-Oct wettest but quietest/cheapest)","booking_lead":"Semana Santa ~1 year; weddings 9-12 months; general dry-season 2-3 months","off_season_specials":"wet-months ''quiet Antigua'' value: coffee-finca/roasting tours, jade & textile workshops, cooking classes, Casa Santo Domingo museums + spa, guided treks with flexible dates","event_peaks":["Semana Santa (late Mar/early Apr)","Sumpango Barriletes Gigantes giant-kite festival (Nov 1, All Saints)","Christmas/New Year"]},"jewels":[{"name":"Acatenango sunrise-over-Fuego overnight","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Guided overnight ridge camp at ~3,500 m watching Fuego erupt through the night and sunrise over the highlands.","bookable_category":"guided overnight trek (guided-only)","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.muchbetteradventures.com/magazine/acatenango-volcano-hike-guide/","timing":"Semana Santa  late Mar/early Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","blurb":"Guided overnight ridge camp at ~3,500 m watching Fuego erupt through the night and sunrise over the highlands.","when":"Semana Santa  late Mar/early Apr","commission":"DMC 10-12% / Viator-GetYourGuide 4-8%; park + guide fees pass-through"},{"name":"Pacaya lava hike + marshmallows","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Shorter guided hike to warm volcanic ground near active Pacaya; family-friendly acclimatizer.","bookable_category":"guided day hike","tier":"essential","source":"https://theworldtravelguy.com/acatenango-hike-volcan-de-fuego/","si":"expedition","blurb":"Shorter guided hike to warm volcanic ground near active Pacaya; family-friendly acclimatizer.","commission":"affiliate 4-8% / DMC 10-12%; park fee pass-through"},{"name":"Semana Santa alfombras + processions","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Dawn Good Friday La Merced procession over street carpets of colored sawdust and flowers - the most famous Holy Week in the Americas.","bookable_category":"event + hotel/DMC room block","tier":"premier","source":"https://livinginguatemala.com/events/semana-santa-guatemala/","timing":"Semana Santa  late Mar/early Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"Dawn Good Friday La Merced procession over street carpets of colored sawdust and flowers - the most famous Holy Week in the Americas.","when":"Semana Santa  late Mar/early Apr","commission":"hotel/DMC AOR; event pass-through; book ~1 yr ahead"},{"name":"Cerro de la Cruz viewpoint","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Hilltop cross with the classic Antigua panorama framed by Volcan Agua.","bookable_category":"free / guided city tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/antigua-guatemala-l1619/from-antigua-or-guatemala-coffee-culture-full-day-tour-t21818/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"Hilltop cross with the classic Antigua panorama framed by Volcan Agua.","when":"year-round","commission":"bundled into commissionable city tour"},{"name":"Santo Domingo del Cerro sculpture park","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Hilltop art-and-garden annex above Casa Santo Domingo with city + volcano views; free hotel shuttle.","bookable_category":"free / hotel shuttle add-on","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.casasantodomingo.com.gt/","timing":"Semana Santa  late Mar/early Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"Hilltop art-and-garden annex above Casa Santo Domingo with city + volcano views; free hotel shuttle.","when":"Semana Santa  late Mar/early Apr","commission":"pairs with Casa Santo Domingo stay (hotel AOR)"},{"name":"Jade museum + workshop","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Working jade ateliers demonstrating Guatemala''s Maya jade tradition; high-margin retail tie-in.","bookable_category":"guided artisan tour","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.dlgcoffee.org/coffee-tour","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"Working jade ateliers demonstrating Guatemala''s Maya jade tradition; high-margin retail tie-in.","when":"year-round","commission":"artisan-tour affiliate; retail non-commissionable"},{"name":"Chichicastenango market day-trip","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Thursday/Sunday highland Maya market of textiles and masks.","bookable_category":"DMC day tour (cleared corridor)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.martsam.com/","timing":"Semana Santa  late Mar/early Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"Thursday/Sunday highland Maya market of textiles and masks.","when":"Semana Santa  late Mar/early Apr","commission":"DMC 10-12% / affiliate 4-8%"},{"name":"Ciudad Vieja (first colonial capital)","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Guatemala''s original 1527 capital, destroyed by a 1541 lahar, just outside Antigua - deep-history layer.","bookable_category":"guided cultural add-on","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/antigua-guatemala-l1619/from-antigua-or-guatemala-coffee-culture-full-day-tour-t21818/","timing":"Semana Santa  late Mar/early Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"Guatemala''s original 1527 capital, destroyed by a 1541 lahar, just outside Antigua - deep-history layer.","when":"Semana Santa  late Mar/early Apr","commission":"bundled into commissionable heritage tour"},{"name":"Finca Filadelfia coffee tour","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"Finca-to-cup tour on an 1870-founded estate, one of Guatemala''s first coffee farms; ~$20, on-site hotel + restaurant.","bookable_category":"coffee-finca tour (direct/Viator)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.visit-antigua.com/finca-filadelfia.php","timing":"Semana Santa  late Mar/early Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","blurb":"Finca-to-cup tour on an 1870-founded estate, one of Guatemala''s first coffee farms; ~$20, on-site hotel + restaurant.","when":"Semana Santa  late Mar/early Apr","commission":"Viator affiliate 4-8%; direct pass-through"},{"name":"De la Gente community coffee tour","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"Nonprofit farmer-led tour in San Miguel Escobar (~4 hr, ~$38 incl. shuttle + beans) - responsible-tourism moat.","bookable_category":"community coffee tour","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.dlgcoffee.org/coffee-tour","timing":"Semana Santa  late Mar/early Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","blurb":"Nonprofit farmer-led tour in San Miguel Escobar (~4 hr, ~$38 incl. shuttle + beans) - responsible-tourism moat.","when":"Semana Santa  late Mar/early Apr","commission":"affiliate/donation model; largely pass-through - brand-values proof point"},{"name":"Guatemalan cooking class","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"Hands-on colonial-kitchen class (pepian, tamales, tortillas); rainy-day-proof culinary depth.","bookable_category":"Viator/GetYourGuide class","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/antigua-guatemala-l1619/from-antigua-or-guatemala-coffee-culture-full-day-tour-t21818/","timing":"Semana Santa  late Mar/early Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","blurb":"Hands-on colonial-kitchen class (pepian, tamales, tortillas); rainy-day-proof culinary depth.","when":"Semana Santa  late Mar/early Apr","commission":"affiliate 4-8%"},{"name":"Sumpango Barriletes Gigantes giant-kite festival","si_tag":"Wildlife & Nature","status":"future","hook":"40-ft+ handmade kites flown in the cemetery on All Saints'' Day (Nov 1) to commune with the dead.","bookable_category":"DMC day tour (Nov 1 only)","tier":"comfort","source":"https://tropicanahostel.com/antigua-weather-what-to-expect-and-the-best-time-to-visit/","timing":"Semana Santa  late Mar/early Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"wildlife","blurb":"40-ft+ handmade kites flown in the cemetery on All Saints'' Day (Nov 1) to commune with the dead.","when":"Semana Santa  late Mar/early Apr","commission":"DMC 10-12% / affiliate 4-8%; entry pass-through"}],"faq":[{"q":"How hard is the Acatenango overnight volcano trek?","a":"It''s a serious guided overnight — roughly 1,570 m of ascent to a 3,976 m summit over a 10–12-hour trek split across two days, with base camp near 3,500 m. It''s worth it because you watch Fuego erupt through the night, but altitude and cold are real, so TWW sells reputable guided operators only.","source":"theworldtravelguy.com, Accessed 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Antigua a good place for a wedding or honeymoon?","a":"Yes — Antigua is a genuinely rising colonial-wedding city, because its converted-palace boutique hotels deliver character at the luxury-boutique level: Casa Santo Domingo (5-star, #11 of 102, 4.6★, 2,724 reviews), palace-suite Palacio de Doña Leonor, and adults-only 26-room Pensativo House. Colonial weddings book 9–12 months ahead.","source":"tripadvisor.com, Accessed 2026-07-06","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"When is Semana Santa 2027 and how far ahead should I book?","a":"Book about a year ahead. Semana Santa 2027 runs ~March 24–28 (Good Friday Mar 26), the most famous Holy Week in the Americas, and Antigua has limited hotel inventory — \"the best places sell out months in advance.\" Fire the booking a full year out, with a \"book by January\" last-call.","source":"livinginguatemala.com, Accessed 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Can I tour a coffee farm from Antigua?","a":"Yes, minutes from the plaza. Finca Filadelfia — founded 1870 as one of Guatemala''s first coffee farms — runs ~2-hour finca-to-cup tours (~$20), and nonprofit De la Gente runs a ~4-hour farmer-led tour in San Miguel Escobar (~$38 incl. shuttle + beans), because Antigua is a premier coffee origin.","source":"visit-antigua.com, Accessed 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"Does Antigua have spa and wellness options?","a":"Yes — the anchor is the 5-star Hotel Museo Spa Casa Santo Domingo, whose spa sits alongside six on-site museums inside 16th-century Dominican monastery ruins, making it Antigua''s iconic wellness-and-culture address. It''s a quiet colonial-retreat market rather than a resort-spa one.","source":"tripadvisor.com, Accessed 2026-07-06","si_tag":"wellness"},{"q":"Can I see the giant-kite festival from Antigua?","a":"Yes, as a Nov 1 day-trip. The Sumpango Barriletes Gigantes festival flies 40-ft+ handmade kites in the cemetery on All Saints'' Day to commune with the dead — visually stunning and uniquely Guatemalan, an easy DMC day tour from Antigua.","source":"tropicanahostel.com, Accessed 2026-07-06","si_tag":"wildlife"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for on Acatenango?","a":"Cold, not lava. Base-camp temperatures drop to 0 °C to −5 °C; on January 8, 2017, six Guatemalan hikers died of hypothermia on Acatenango after arriving unprepared — an exposure/preparation failure, not a lava event. Book only reputable guided operators who supply proper down layers, tents and a real sleeping system.","source":"theworldtravelguy.com, Accessed 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Antigua Guatemala Travel Guide 2026 — Volcanoes, Semana Santa & Colonial Weddings | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Plan Antigua Guatemala: the Acatenango/Fuego overnight volcano trek (guided-only, 3,976 m), world-famous Semana Santa alfombras, coffee fincas, colonial-wedding hotels, and straight L3 State-Dept-cleared safety.","slug":"antigua-guatemala","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-06","search_language":["en","es-GT"],"local_keywords":["qué hacer en Antigua Guatemala","Acatenango tour","Semana Santa Antigua","bodas Antigua Guatemala","tour de café Antigua","volcán Pacaya Antigua","hoteles de lujo Antigua Guatemala","alfombras Semana Santa"],"hreflang":["en","es-GT"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"expedition","status":"live"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"culinary","status":"future"},{"si":"wildlife","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Hotel Museo Spa Casa Santo Domingo","why_ultra":"5-star in 16th-c. Dominican monastery ruins; six museums + spa; #11 of 102 Antigua hotels; Antigua''s iconic top-of-market address","earning":"on application / host-Virtuoso or Fora where eligible","virtuoso_value_add":"consortia amenities where eligible (verify)","mor":true,"tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Palacio de Dona Leonor","why_ultra":"converted colonial palace, antique-furnished grand suites in the historic core; romance/honeymoon standout","earning":"on application / Fora lane where eligible","virtuoso_value_add":"consortia amenities where eligible (verify)","mor":true,"tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Pensativo House","why_ultra":"26-room adults-only boutique (Porta Hotels), garden + rooftop + spa, steps off Central Park; honeymoon fit","earning":"on application / Fora lane","virtuoso_value_add":"consortia amenities where eligible (verify)","mor":true,"tier":"luxury"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Antigua, Guatemala"},"geo":{"lat":14.5586,"lng":-90.7295}}'::jsonb, 32)
