mingo de los Tsáchilas This does not apply to airside transit within Guayaquil Airport in Guayas province."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km of the Ecuador-Colombia border, except for these areas in Carchi province: El Ángel Ecological Reserve Rumichaca border crossing the town of Tulcán the Pan-American Highway Find out more about why FCDO advises against travel ."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to Guayaquil, except for airside transit through the airport."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to those provinces) and get local advice on where to visit."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Coastal Region provinces of: Esmeraldas Manabi Santa Elena El Oro Los Ríos Santo Domingo de los Tsáchilas This is due to a high level of gang-related violence linked to the presence of organised crime relating to the production and trafficking of illegal drugs."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to the Coastal Region province of Guayas, except: airside transit within Guayaquil Airport in Guayas province."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel to areas within 20km of the Ecuador-Colombia border, except for these areas in Carchi province: El Ángel Ecological Reserve Rumichaca border crossing the town of Tulcán the Pan-American Highway This is due to the presence of organised crime linked to the production and trafficking of drugs."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ecuador","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-07-10T10:44:44+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak":["Sep","Oct","Nov","Dec","Jan","Feb"],"shoulder_green":["Mar","Apr","May","Jun","Jul","Aug"],"inflection":["Aug","Feb","Mar"],"fire_date":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks (mid-Aug for the Sep-Feb dry peak; 1-2 weeks ahead of Ecuadorian holiday weekends/Carnaval/Semana Santa); fire against the arriving Quito curve when Baños rides as an Andes/Amazon attach","events":["Ecuadorian national holiday weekends (feriados) — domestic-demand spikes","Carnaval (Feb-Mar)","Semana Santa"],"rafting_note":"Pastaza Class III+ year-round; Class IV seasonal (~Aug-May)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Casa del Árbol — Swing at the End of the World","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/Banos-attractions/Casa-del-Arbol-Swing/d22150-a19710","timing":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the iconic treehouse swing on the Runtún ridge, launching out over the Tungurahua gorge; entry ~$1, 07:00–19:00, harness-secured, 18+","si":"expedition","blurb":"the iconic treehouse swing on the Runtún ridge, launching out over the Tungurahua gorge; entry ~$1, 07:00–19:00, harness-secured, 18+","when":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","commission":"Guided swing/viewpoint tour affiliate or DMC leg (entry non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Pailón del Diablo (Devil''s Cauldron waterfall)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.zoegoesplaces.com/cascada-el-pailon-del-diablo-ecuador/","timing":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"is one of Ecuador''s most dramatic waterfalls — roughly 80 m tall with a plunge pool ~20 m deep","si":"expedition","blurb":"is one of Ecuador''s most dramatic waterfalls — roughly 80 m tall with a plunge pool ~20 m deep","when":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","commission":"Ruta de las Cascadas day-trip affiliate/DMC (trail entry non-comm.)"},{"name":"Ruta de las Cascadas (bike / chiva)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://southamericabackpacker.com/ruta-de-las-cascadas-banos/","hook":"~16 km of seven waterfalls downhill from Baños along the Pastaza","si":"expedition","blurb":"~16 km of seven waterfalls downhill from Baños along the Pastaza","commission":"Bike-hire + guided-route/chiva-tour affiliate (fall/cable fees non-comm.)"},{"name":"Canyoning — Río Blanco","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.geotoursbanios.com/","timing":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","when":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","commission":"Local adventure-operator booking (Geotours/Ivagatours) — guided-only"},{"name":"Whitewater rafting — Río Pastaza (Class III-IV)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/Banos-tours/White-Water-Rafting/d22150-g17-c27534","timing":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"half-day guided runs; Class III+ year-round, Class IV seasonal; PFD + helmet + river guide","si":"expedition","blurb":"half-day guided runs; Class III+ year-round, Class IV seasonal; PFD + helmet + river guide","when":"[''Sep'', ''Oct'', ''Nov'', ''Dec'', ''Jan'', ''Feb'']","commission":"Local operator + activity affiliate"},{"name":"Mirador Bellavista","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.ecuatouring.com/banos-travel-guide/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"a short, steep hike for the postcard panorama of Baños in its gorge with Tungurahua behind — a free, romantic sunset jewel","si":"expedition","blurb":"a short, steep hike for the postcard panorama of Baños in its gorge with Tungurahua behind — a free, romantic sunset jewel","when":"year-round","commission":"Guided town-and-viewpoint walk affiliate or self-guided add-on"},{"name":"Termas de la Virgen thermal baths (at night)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g312857-d20120113-Reviews-Termas_de_la_Virgen-Banos_Tungurahua_Province.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"soak in Tungurahua-heated, sulfate-rich mineral pools in the town center, beneath the floodlit Cabellera de la Virgen waterfall; open into the evening, ~$4 entry","si":"romance","blurb":"soak in Tungurahua-heated, sulfate-rich mineral pools in the town center, beneath the floodlit Cabellera de la Virgen waterfall; open into the evening, ~$4 entry","when":"year-round","commission":"Entry non-commissionable — monetize spa-hotel room-night + private spa add-on"},{"name":"Luna Volcán / former Luna Runtún — spa with volcano view","si_tag":"romance","tier":"luxury","source":"https://www.booking.com/hotel/ec/luna-volcan-adventure-spa.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"perched on Tungurahua''s flank on 35 ha of Andean forest, infinity pool over the valley, themed suites; the marquee romantic-adventure perch above Baños","si":"romance","blurb":"perched on Tungurahua''s flank on 35 ha of Andean forest, infinity pool over the valley, themed suites; the marquee romantic-adventure perch above Baños","when":"year-round","commission":"Direct/luxury-specialist + bedbank; property/wing buyout for weddings"},{"name":"Samari Spa Resort (converted monastery)","si_tag":"wellness","tier":"luxury","source":"https://www.luxurylatinamerica.com/ecuador/samari.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"wellness","when":"year-round","commission":"Direct/luxury-specialist + bedbank — future Wellness SI anchor"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is the \"Swing at the End of the World\" worth it — and how much?","a":"Yes, and it is cheap — it is the image that put Baños on a million screens. The Casa del Árbol treehouse swing launches you out over the Tungurahua gorge from the Runtún ridge at ~2,600 m; the complex opens 07:00–19:00, entry is ~$1, and staff clip you into a climbing harness on a steel-beam frame.","source":"viator.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Where can couples soak in thermal baths at night in Baños?","a":"At the Termas de la Virgen, in the town center beneath the floodlit Cabellera de la Virgen waterfall. Its sulfate-rich pools are heated by Tungurahua, open 05:00–17:00 and again 18:00–22:00, at ~$4 adult entry — the signature romantic-and-restorative Baños ritual, best paired with a volcano-view spa-hotel room-night.","source":"tripadvisor.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Is Baños a genuine wellness and spa destination?","a":"Increasingly, yes — the town''s name literally means \"Baths of Holy Water.\" The anchor is Samari Spa Resort, a 300-year-old former Jesuit monastery on ~10 acres with a heated indoor pool, sauna, Turkish bath, whirlpool and full spa, ranked among Baños''s top hotels — mineral-rich thermal springs fed by Tungurahua''s volcanic heat make Baños a natural wellness base.","source":"luxurylatinamerica.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"wellness-—-future-si"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Baños?","a":"Not urban crime — the load-bearing risk is activity risk. ~88% of Ecuador''s homicides occur in five coastal provinces, and the Andean highlands including Baños run below the homicide rates of many mid-sized US cities; the town''s core product is adrenaline (canyoning, Class III–IV rafting, the swing, highway cycling), so guided-vs-unguided is the whole game.","source":"myecuadorvisa.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is the Tungurahua volcano dangerous right now?","a":"It is a real, live geohazard held quiet by monitoring — not a decorative caveat. Tungurahua erupted near-continuously 1999–2016, then went quiet; as of mid-2026 IG-EPN reports background/very-low activity with no precursor signals and 24/7 instrument monitoring, so any escalation would trigger alerts well in advance. Re-verify live IG-EPN status before booking.","source":"igepn.edu.ec, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is canyoning or the swing in Baños dangerous?","a":"Both carry real, activity-specific risk that guiding and gear mitigate. Canyoning on the Río Blanco is a guided-only roped waterfall-descent sport (helmet, harness, wetsuit, certified guide); the Casa del Árbol swing is 18+ with a ~220 lb (100 kg) weight limit and requires the operator''s climbing harness every ride. Never freelance either — book reputable operators like Geotours or Ivagatours.","source":"geotoursbanios.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Baños de Agua Santa, Ecuador — The Swing, Waterfalls, Rafting & Thermal Baths | TravelWell","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-EC","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Baños Ecuador","Casa del Árbol columpio","columpio fin del mundo Baños","Pailón del Diablo","Ruta de las Cascadas","rafting río Pastaza Baños","canyoning Baños","Termas de la Virgen","volcán Tungurahua estado","hoteles con spa en Baños"],"hreflang":["en","es-EC"],"primary_keyword":"Baños de Agua Santa"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"wellness","status":"live"},{"si":"romance","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Luna Volcán, Adventure SPA (formerly Luna Runtún)","category":"Boutique adventure-spa on Tungurahua''s flank, 30 rooms, 35-ha forest","mor":"Luxury-specialist / direct trade + bedbank; Fora/host-agency on direct","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Samari Spa Resort","category":"300-yr converted-monastery spa resort, ~10 acres","mor":"Luxury-specialist / direct trade + bedbank; host-agency/Fora on direct","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Casa del Suizo","category":"Amazon-edge Napo River jungle lodge (Ahuano), 75 rooms","mor":"DMC package / luxury-specialist — the Amazon-extend upsell","tier":"$$$-$$$$"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Baños de Agua Santa, Ecuador, Ecuador"},"geo":{"lat":-1.3928,"lng":-78.4269}}'::jsonb, 36),
  ('bogota-colombia', '10S', 'Bogotá & The Andes, Colombia', 'Colombia', 'Andean capital, paramo on its doorstep', 'live', 'verified', 'venice', 'Bogotá & The Andes', '{"romance","adventure","culture","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Bogotá sits at ~2,640 m (8,660 ft) — one of the highest capital cities on earth; expect mild soroche (altitude effects) for 24–48 hrs on arrival.","The Gold Museum (Museo del Oro) holds ~55,000 pre-Columbian gold pieces, incl. the Muisca raft of the El Dorado legend.","Monserrate rises to 3,152 m over the city, reached by funicular, cable car or a steep daytime walk, with the Basilica at the summit.","Zipaquirá Salt Cathedral is a cathedral carved inside a working salt mine ~1.5–2 hrs from the city; Villa de Leyva has Colombia''s largest cobbled plaza (14,000 m²) and a Cretaceous fossil valley.","Bogotá''s driest, clearest windows are Dec–Mar and Jul–Aug; the biennial Ibero-American Theatre Festival returns August 2026."],"safety":{"emergency":"123","hospital":"Bogotá top private clinics (stabilization); serious cases route to US medical evacuation — evac-grade insurance advised","book_enabled":true,"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","risk_codes":["C","T","U","K","N"],"risk_code_meanings":{"C":"Crime — violent crime (murder, assault, robbery), drugging (scopolamine/''devil''s breath''), extortion, express kidnapping occur throughout Colombia incl. cities","T":"Terrorism — attacks possible with little/no warning; car bombs, grenades, IEDs, drones","U":"Unrest — demonstrations can shut roads and turn violent","K":"Kidnapping or Hostage-Taking — kidnapping-for-ransom reported","N":"Natural Disaster — earthquake, landslide (advisory names Bogotá for landslide risk)"},"named_danger":["Arauca","Cauca excl Popayán","Valle del Cauca excl Cali","Norte de Santander","Venezuela border ~10km"],"bogota_in_named_danger":false,"consent_flow":{"bin":"BOOK WITH WARNING","disclosure_required":true,"renders":"full verbatim live US State Dept advisory for Colombia (level + reason + named-danger areas + complete ''If you decide to travel'' guidance, pulled live) + traveler acknowledgment","wording_status":"hook set only — final consent language PENDING compliance-attorney sign-off"},"air_access_verified":"BOG (El Dorado Intl) — direct international incl. major US, EU and LatAm gateways; Colombia''s primary hub","altitude_m":2640,"altitude_note":"~2,640 m — mild AMS possible 24–48 hrs; Monserrate 3,152 m and páramo hikes 3,200 m+ add load","water":"Bogotá tap generally potable (meets WHO standards per EAAB/Ministry of Health); caveat aging plumbing in older buildings — bottled is conservative default","disease_note":"dengue LOW at altitude (vector scarce above ~1,800 m); rises for low-altitude excursions","scopolamine_caution":"''devil''s breath''/burundanga drugging — colourless/tasteless; Bogotá hotspot (1,409 cases 2023, Chapinero/Teusaquillo/Santa Fe); never accept drinks/food/tabs from strangers; dating-app method documented","personal_safety":"vetted taxi/ride-app only; no wealth display; zone discipline (La Candelaria daytime); do not resist a robbery"},"timing":{"peak":"Dec–Mar (dry, peak season) and Jul–Aug (dry + biennial Ibero-American Theatre Festival, even years)","inflection_curve_start":"early December (Christmas peak); August 2026 (Theatre Festival + dry season); Semana Santa (late Mar/early Apr)","fire_date":"mid-to-late November (Dec–Mar peak); ~mid-July (Aug festival/dry peak); ~early March (Semana Santa)","event_peaks":[{"event":"Ibero-American Theatre Festival","dates_2026":"August 2026 (biennial, even years)","note":"800+ productions from 40+ countries; stacks on dry season"},{"event":"Semana Santa (Holy Week)","dates":"late March / early April","note":"major domestic-travel pulse across the Andes"},{"event":"Christmas–New Year","dates":"Dec 20–Jan 6","note":"peak congestion + higher rates"}],"off_season_fill":"Apr–May and Oct–Nov (green/wetter shoulders, lower rates, thinner crowds)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Gold Museum (Museo del Oro)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.viator.com/Bogota-attractions/Gold-Museum/d4560-a6188","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"~55,000 pre-Columbian gold pieces, the Muisca raft of the El Dorado legend; free on Sundays","si":"culture","blurb":"~55,000 pre-Columbian gold pieces, the Muisca raft of the El Dorado legend; free on Sundays","when":"year-round","commission":"city-tour affiliate; entry non-comm pass-through"},{"name":"Botero Museum","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://theabroadguide.com/la-candelaria-mount-monserrate-and-the-gold-museum-in-one-day-in-bogota/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"Fernando Botero''s donated collection, free entry, in La Candelaria","si":"culture","blurb":"Fernando Botero''s donated collection, free entry, in La Candelaria","when":"year-round","commission":"city-tour affiliate; free entry"},{"name":"La Candelaria colonial core + street art","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://kittiaroundtheworld.com/things-to-do-in-la-candelaria-bogota-historic-centre/","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Plaza de Bolívar, 17th-c. Iglesia de Santa Clara, mural-covered lanes, the number-one neighbourhood in the city","si":"culture","blurb":"Plaza de Bolívar, 17th-c. Iglesia de Santa Clara, mural-covered lanes, the number-one neighbourhood in the city","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"walking-tour affiliate + boutique lodging"},{"name":"Zipaquirá Salt Cathedral","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://thecolombianway.com/en/our-trips/day-trips/the-salt-cathedral-of-zipaquira/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"a cathedral carved inside a working salt mine, glowing tunnels, carved crosses, an underground dome; ~1.5–2 hrs from Bogotá","si":"culture","blurb":"a cathedral carved inside a working salt mine, glowing tunnels, carved crosses, an underground dome; ~1.5–2 hrs from Bogotá","when":"year-round","commission":"day-trip DMC/operator; entry non-comm pass-through"},{"name":"Villa de Leyva (colonial plaza + fossils)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"premier","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Villa_de_Leyva","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"a whitewashed-town weekend around the great plaza, star-filled Andean skies, boutique fincas — the plateau''s romance run","si":"culture","blurb":"a whitewashed-town weekend around the great plaza, star-filled Andean skies, boutique fincas — the plateau''s romance run","when":"year-round","commission":"overnight DMC + colonial-house/finca villa MoR"},{"name":"Monserrate sunset (funicular/cable car)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"premier","source":"https://kittiaroundtheworld.com/things-to-do-in-la-candelaria-bogota-historic-centre/","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"hotel + funicular non-comm + DMC dining"},{"name":"Usaquén Sunday market + brunch","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g294074-d1382992-Reviews-Mercado_de_las_Pulgas_de_Usaquen-Bogota.html","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the colonial northern district; every Sunday ~10:00–18:00 the streets fill with artisans, antiques, Colombian coffee and long brunches around the plaza","si":"romance","blurb":"the colonial northern district; every Sunday ~10:00–18:00 the streets fill with artisans, antiques, Colombian coffee and long brunches around the plaza","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"boutique-lodging + food-tour affiliate"},{"name":"Chingaza páramo hike","si_tag":"adventure","tier":"premier","source":"https://mytriptocolombia.com/hiking-chingaza-national-park-travel-guide/","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"a magnificent páramo on Bogotá''s outskirts, frailejón moorland, glacial Siecha/Buitrago lagoons, guided day trips from the city","si":"adventure","blurb":"a magnificent páramo on Bogotá''s outskirts, frailejón moorland, glacial Siecha/Buitrago lagoons, guided day trips from the city","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"GEA DMC / licensed guide + park permit"},{"name":"Suesca rock-climbing","si_tag":"adventure","tier":"essential","source":"https://cuppatocopatravels.com/south-america/colombia/day-trips-weekend-breaks-from-bogota-2019/","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Colombia''s best climbing crag, ~1 hr north; sandstone canyon walls, beginner-to-advanced routes through local climbing schools","si":"adventure","blurb":"Colombia''s best climbing crag, ~1 hr north; sandstone canyon walls, beginner-to-advanced routes through local climbing schools","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"adventure DMC / climbing-school affiliate"},{"name":"Sumapaz páramo trek","si_tag":"adventure","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/articles/day-hikes-bogota-colombia","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the world''s largest páramo ecosystem, south of Bogotá; high-altitude moorland trekking, guided-only","si":"adventure","blurb":"the world''s largest páramo ecosystem, south of Bogotá; high-altitude moorland trekking, guided-only","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"GEA DMC / licensed guide (guided-only)"},{"name":"Paloquemao market + coffee","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"essential","source":"https://theabroadguide.com/la-candelaria-mount-monserrate-and-the-gold-museum-in-one-day-in-bogota/","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Bogotá''s great produce, flower and food market; early-morning fruit tastings and Colombian-coffee sourcing, a food-tour anchor","si":"culinary","blurb":"Bogotá''s great produce, flower and food market; early-morning fruit tastings and Colombian-coffee sourcing, a food-tour anchor","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"food-tour affiliate + DMC"},{"name":"Andrés Carne de Res (Chía)","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/Restaurant_Review-g815502-d939879-Reviews-Andres_Carne_De_Res_Chia-Chia_Cundinamarca_Department.html","timing":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the legendary maximalist restaurant ~40–60 min north of Bogotá — a labyrinth of over-the-top décor, live music and improv actors","si":"culinary","blurb":"the legendary maximalist restaurant ~40–60 min north of Bogotá — a labyrinth of over-the-top décor, live music and improv actors","when":"Dec–Mar  and Jul–Aug","commission":"DMC dining + vetted transport"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the most romantic thing to do in Bogotá?","a":"Ride the funicular or cable car up Monserrate at dusk for dinner at the summit restaurant, with the whole plateau of light beneath you — the city''s signature romance run. The ridge rises to 3,152 m (10,341 ft), and the Basilica crowns the summit.","source":"kittiaroundtheworld.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you go hiking near Bogotá?","a":"Yes — Andean páramo day-hikes start on the city''s doorstep and run guided. Chingaza páramo climbs from 2,600 to 4,000 m through frailejón moorland and glacial Siecha/Buitrago lagoons, while Suesca, about 1 hour north, is Colombia''s premier rock-climbing crag. Guided entry is the norm for the páramos.","source":"mytriptocolombia.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"adventure"},{"q":"What are the must-see museums and sights in Bogotá?","a":"The Gold Museum (Museo del Oro) is the headline — ~55,000 pre-Columbian gold pieces, including the Muisca raft of the El Dorado legend, and free on Sundays — alongside the Botero Museum and colonial La Candelaria. The core clusters in and above the historic centre.","source":"viator.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Where should you eat and drink around Bogotá?","a":"Andrés Carne de Res in Chía is the marquee night out — ranked #2 of 139 restaurants in Chía, a labyrinth of over-the-top décor, live music and improv actors, about 40–60 min north of the city. In town, Zona G is Bogotá''s dense \"gourmet zone.\"","source":"tripadvisor.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Bogotá?","a":"Scopolamine (\"devil''s breath\" / burundanga) drugging is the headline traveler risk — a colourless, tasteless sedative used to rob or assault. Bogotá police recorded 1,409 cases in 2023 (+16% year-on-year), concentrated in Chapinero, Teusaquillo and Santa Fe, often via dating apps and offered drinks. Never accept drinks or tabs from strangers.","source":"thecitypaperbogota.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is walking up Monserrate dangerous?","a":"Walk the Monserrate pilgrimage trail only in daylight and in groups — robberies have been reported on the path — or take the funicular or cable car instead. The summit stands at 3,152 m, so pace yourself for the altitude.","source":"kittiaroundtheworld.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Bogotá & The Andes, Colombia — Gold Museum, Monserrate, Zipaquirá & Villa de Leyva | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-CO","long_tail_en":["things to do in Bogotá Colombia","Gold Museum Bogotá guide","Monserrate funicular Bogotá","Zipaquirá Salt Cathedral day trip from Bogotá","Villa de Leyva from Bogotá","is Bogotá safe 2026","Bogotá altitude sickness"],"local_keywords":["qué hacer en Bogotá","Catedral de Sal Zipaquirá","Museo del Oro","Villa de Leyva","Monserrate Bogotá","hoteles de lujo Bogotá"],"hreflang":["en","es-CO"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":["romance","adventure","culture","culinary"],"ultra":[{"name":"Four Seasons Hotel Casa Medina","type":"landmark 1946 building, Zona G, 62 rooms + 19 suites, Ministry-of-Culture monument","routing":"Fora/Virtuoso preferred","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Four Seasons Hotel Bogotá","type":"second FS property, Zona T entertainment district, contemporary tower","routing":"Fora/Virtuoso preferred","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Sofitel Bogotá Victoria Regia","type":"French-luxury prestige address, northern corridor","routing":"preferred-partner + host","tier":"luxury→ultra"},{"name":"W Bogotá (Zona T)","type":"Marriott lifestyle-luxury flagship, design-forward rooftop","routing":"preferred-partner + host","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Click Clack Hotel","type":"design-forward boutique, northern corridor","routing":"preferred-partner + host","tier":"premium→luxury"},{"name":"Zona G / Chicó luxury-apartment buyouts","type":"serviced multi-bedroom apartments w/ concierge","routing":"MoR villa + host","tier":"premier"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Bogotá & The Andes, Colombia, Colombia"},"geo":{"lat":4.711,"lng":-74.0721}}'::jsonb, 37),
  ('bonito-brazil', '10S', 'Bonito, Brazil', 'Brazil', 'Bonito', 'live', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Amazon, Pantanal & Iguaçu', '{"wildlife"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"190","advisory_level":"L2","advisory_why":"national crime + kidnapping risk indicator concentrated in cities, favelas, and Level-4 border zones — none describe interior Bonito","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L2)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":true,"air_access":{"primary":"Bonito (BYO) — limited commercial service (~13 km from town)","gateway":"Campo Grande (CGR) + road transfer ~205 km / ~3–3.5 hrs"},"trauma_note":"rural interior; serious-trauma/evac route via Campo Grande (CGR); evacuation-coverage insurance essential for adventure stack","health_flag":"chikungunya outbreak reported in Mato Grosso do Sul — mosquito-bite prevention day and night","activity_flags":["river no-touch + no pre-entry sunscreen","cave/waterfall rappel technical + harness","cool water ~18–22°C neoprene"],"fcdo":{"posture":"AREA-RESTRICTED","quotes":[{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel Amazonas State FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the following river areas towards the west of Amazonas State: along the Amazonas (Amazon) River and its tributaries west of the town of Codajás and east of the town of Belém do Solimões in Amazonas State along any part of the Itaquaí River in Amazonas State along any part of the Japurá River or its tributaries in Amazonas State along the Rio Negro (Black River) and its tributaries north or west of the town of Barcelos in Amazonas State Find out more about why FCDO advises against travel ."},{"form":"against all but essential travel","text":"advises against all but essential travel: along the Amazonas (Amazon) River and its tributaries west of the town of Codajás and east of the town of Belém do Solimões in Amazonas State along any part of the Itaquaí River in Amazonas State along any part of the Japurá River or its tributaries in Amazonas State along the Rio Negro (Black River) and its tributaries north or west of the town of Barcelos in Amazonas State There are risks to travellers in river areas towards the west of Amazonas State, where Brazil shares borders with Colombia, Peru and Venezuela, due to criminal activity."}],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/brazil","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-05-11T12:32:48+01:00"}},"timing":{"clarity_peak":"dry season ~Apr–Oct (core Jun–Sep)","crowd_price_peak":"December → Carnival","low_visibility_window":"Dec–Feb (rain raises rivers)","shoulder":"Mar–Jun (milder, fewer crowds)","inflection":"supply is physically day-capped; slots close weeks ahead in dry window","fire_date":"clarity-curve start − 1–2 weeks (late Mar–May for winter clarity trips; Oct–Nov ahead of Dec–Carnival)","off_season_fill":"dry low-season tail + wet-but-workable shoulder → flexible/budget/photography travelers","note":"attractions sell out, not just hotels — book the voucher itinerary"},"jewels":[{"name":"Rio da Prata float","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g303368-d1936985-r118728253-Rio_da_Prata-State_of_Mato_Grosso_do_Sul.html","si":"expedition","commission":"DMC/AOR → licensed-agency voucher"},{"name":"Rio Sucuri snorkel","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.aventuradobrasil.com/blog/bonito-brazils-natural-gem-of-crystal-clear-rivers-and-hidden-caves/","hook":"Described as one of the clearest rivers on Earth; emerald underwater gardens threaded with pearl-like oxygen bubbles. Gentler/shorter than Prata, superb clarity","si":"expedition","blurb":"Described as one of the clearest rivers on Earth; emerald underwater gardens threaded with pearl-like oxygen bubbles. Gentler/shorter than Prata, superb clarity","commission":"licensed-agency voucher via AOR"},{"name":"Abismo Anhumas rappel + underground-lake dive/snorkel","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.explore-share.com/trip/abismo-anhumas-abseiling-underground-lake-bonito/","hook":"72 m descent into a cavern lake with submerged limestone cones up to ~20 m; snorkel or scuba the lake; ~18°C water","si":"expedition","blurb":"72 m descent into a cavern lake with submerged limestone cones up to ~20 m; snorkel or scuba the lake; ~18°C water","commission":"AOR → operator via licensed agency"},{"name":"Boca da Onça waterfall circuit + 90m rappel","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.bocadaonca.com.br/","hook":"Mato Grosso do Sul''s tallest waterfall; Brazil''s largest platform rappel; ~4,500 m trail, 8 waterfalls, natural pools","si":"expedition","blurb":"Mato Grosso do Sul''s tallest waterfall; Brazil''s largest platform rappel; ~4,500 m trail, 8 waterfalls, natural pools","commission":"AOR → licensed-agency voucher"},{"name":"Estância Mimosa waterfall trek","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.aventuradobrasil.com/blog/bonito-brazils-natural-gem-of-crystal-clear-rivers-and-hidden-caves/","hook":"Guided trail to a chain of waterfalls and swimming pools with strong flora/fauna viewing; also offers on-site lodging","si":"expedition","blurb":"Guided trail to a chain of waterfalls and swimming pools with strong flora/fauna viewing; also offers on-site lodging","commission":"AOR → voucher + room"},{"name":"Gruta do Lago Azul","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gruta_do_Lago_Azul_Natural_Monument","hook":"Guided-mandatory, no swimming. ~300-step descent; closed-toe shoes mandatory; no water access since 1992; the risk here is the stairs, not the water","si":"expedition","blurb":"Guided-mandatory, no swimming. ~300-step descent; closed-toe shoes mandatory; no water access since 1992; the risk here is the stairs, not the water","commission":"voucher via licensed agency; entry fee pass-through"},{"name":"Buraco das Araras (macaw sinkhole)","si_tag":"wildlife","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buraco_das_Araras_Private_Natural_Heritage_Reserve","hook":"Huge sandstone crater near Jardim; South America''s largest sinkhole; sanctuary for red-and-green macaws plus toucans/araçaris. Best at early morning / late afternoon","si":"wildlife","blurb":"Huge sandstone crater near Jardim; South America''s largest sinkhole; sanctuary for red-and-green macaws plus toucans/araçaris. Best at early morning / late afternoon","commission":"AOR → licensed reserve access"},{"name":"Night float","si_tag":"wildlife","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.livemoretravelmore.com/things-to-do-in-bonito-brazil/","si":"wildlife","commission":"licensed-agency voucher"},{"name":"Pantanal wildlife extension (gateway)","si_tag":"wildlife","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.aventuradobrasil.com/blog/bonito-brazils-natural-gem-of-crystal-clear-rivers-and-hidden-caves/","hook":"The high-value pairing: Bonito''s clear water + Pantanal''s unmatched wildlife density. Same regional DMC can carry both","si":"wildlife","blurb":"The high-value pairing: Bonito''s clear water + Pantanal''s unmatched wildlife density. Same regional DMC can carry both","commission":"AOR combo mandate (Bonito + Pantanal)"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is the best time to snorkel Bonito''s crystal rivers?","a":"The dry season — roughly June–September, within the broader May–September dry window — delivers the clearest, most predictable water, because the winter rains that raise rivers and drop visibility have stopped; daily visitor slots are physically capped, so book at least a week ahead in high season (July–September).","source":"lonelyplanet.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Can you actually see wild macaws near Bonito?","a":"Yes — Buraco das Araras, South America''s largest sinkhole (~500 m circumference, ~100 m deep) near Jardim, is a heavily regulated sanctuary for red-and-green macaws plus toucans and araçaris, best viewed at early morning or late afternoon on a guided visit.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"wildlife"},{"q":"Is Bonito a good honeymoon destination?","a":"Yes, as a slow water-and-forest romance add-on rather than a luxury-ceremony market: the top of the market is the 4-star Zagaia Eco Resort — grounds, pools and full recreation — with boutique eco-pousadas filling the couples tier, so set expectations to best-in-region eco, not five-star.","source":"evendo.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Is the Abismo Anhumas cave rappel dangerous?","a":"It is a serious, technical activity run safely under a guided-mandatory system: a 72 m harness rappel on electric devices into a cavern lake (~18°C water, submerged cones to ~20 m), capped at a maximum of 16 people per day with certified monitors — never a free-climb and never sold unguided.","source":"explore-share.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Bonito?","a":"Sell-outs, not danger: because every attraction runs on a licensed-agency voucher with hard daily caps, marquee tours like Rio da Prata and Rio Sucuri can sell out weeks ahead of time, so the booking *is* the reservation — reserve the voucher itinerary, not just the room.","source":"en.wikivoyage.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Bonito, Brazil: Crystal-River Snorkeling, Caves & the Pantanal Gateway — TravelWell","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"pt-BR","local_keywords":["Bonito MS o que fazer","Rio da Prata flutuação","Gruta do Lago Azul","melhor época para ir a Bonito","Abismo Anhumas rapel","Boca da Onça cachoeira","Bonito e Pantanal roteiro","Buraco das Araras Jardim"],"hreflang":["en","pt-BR"],"primary_keyword":"Bonito"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"wildlife","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Zagaia Eco Resort","positioning":"4-star Bonito ceiling","earning":"room commission","mor":"DMC/AOR","tier":"Premium (regional ceiling)"},{"name":"Santa Esmeralda","positioning":"upper-boutique eco-pousada","earning":"room commission / bedbank","mor":"AOR/bedbank","tier":"Premium-lite"},{"name":"Boutique eco-pousadas (curated)","positioning":"design-forward small pousadas — premier eco ceiling, not 5-star","earning":"room commission","mor":"AOR/bedbank","tier":"Mid → Premium-lite"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Bonito, Brazil, Brazil"},"geo":{"lat":-21.1261,"lng":-56.4514}}'::jsonb, 38),
  ('buenos-aires-argentina', '10S', 'Buenos Aires, Argentina', 'Argentina', 'Leather and silk, beef and fire', 'live', 'verified', 'paris', 'Buenos Aires & The Pampas', '{"romance","culture","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["US State Dept Level 1 - Exercise Normal Precautions (advisory dated 2026-05-20); Rosario is a city-level L2 exception, not on a BA itinerary.","Best experience = spring/fall shoulder (Oct-Nov, Mar-Apr); November brings jacaranda bloom + the Argentine Open Polo.","Signature BA experiences: milonga tango, puerta-cerrada (closed-door) asado, Malbec tasting, Recoleta Cemetery (Evita), Teatro Colon.","Day-trip belt: Tigre Delta (~1 hr), San Antonio de Areco estancia (~1.5 hr), Colonia/Uruguay ferry across the Rio de la Plata.","Petty crime is theft-by-distraction, not force (motochorros, ~90% at traffic lights); La Boca daytime-and-Caminito only; tap water potable."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","police":"101","ambulance":"107","fire":"100","us_embassy_ba":"+54 11 5777-4354","advisory_level":"L1","book_enabled":true,"bin":"freely bookable (L1)","consent_flow":false,"air_access_verified":{"international":"EZE (Ezeiza / Ministro Pistarini)","domestic":"AEP (Aeroparque Jorge Newbery)"},"water":"potable","trauma_path":"BA private hospitals excellent; stabilize locally then US medevac for catastrophic cases","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/argentina","read":"2026-08-19","page_updated":"2026-05-07T17:26:11+01:00"}},"timing":{"peak_experience":"Oct-Nov and Mar-Apr (shoulder — best weather/crowds)","peak_volume":"Dec-Feb (austral summer — hot/humid, least comfortable)","inflection_curve_start":"loads ahead of each shoulder window + Nov events","fire_date":"curve-start minus 1-2 weeks (~early Sep for Oct-Nov; ~January for Mar-Apr); November premium = 3-6 months lead","events":[{"name":"Argentine Open Polo Championship","month":"November","venue":"Campo Argentino de Polo, Palermo"},{"name":"Tango BA Festival y Mundial","month":"August (austral winter — NOT November)"}],"low_season":"Jun-Aug (winter; occupancy low ~Apr-Jun — value window)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Private milonga tango night","si_tag":"romance","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/buenos-aires-l1/","hook":"The real social tango — a couple''s night at an authentic milonga beats any tourist stage show for a honeymoon","si":"romance","blurb":"The real social tango — a couple''s night at an authentic milonga beats any tourist stage show for a honeymoon","commission":"activities affiliate / DMC private experience"},{"name":"Recoleta jacarandas + Recoleta Cemetery (Evita tomb)","si_tag":"RHN / Culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.buenosairesfreewalks.com/what-to-do/grave-of-evita-peron/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"A November walk through Recoleta''s lilac-blossom boulevards into the most famous cemetery in the Americas","si":"RHN / Culture","blurb":"A November walk through Recoleta''s lilac-blossom boulevards into the most famous cemetery in the Americas","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC/guide (entry non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Closed-door (puerta cerrada) asado — Fogon Asado","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/buenos-aires-l1/buenos-aires-8-course-argentine-bbq-at-fogon-asado-t235877/","hook":"The most intimate, most Porteño dinner in the city — see Culinary below; sells beautifully as a honeymoon night","si":"culinary","blurb":"The most intimate, most Porteño dinner in the city — see Culinary below; sells beautifully as a honeymoon night","commission":"activities affiliate / DMC"},{"name":"Casa Saltshaker puerta cerrada + Malbec flight","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"comfort","source":"https://theculturetrip.com/south-america/argentina/articles/the-best-closed-door-restaurants-in-buenos-aires","hook":"Intimate shared-table five-course dinners with Malbec-vs-Patagonian-pinot flights — one of the city''s oldest supper clubs","si":"culinary","blurb":"Intimate shared-table five-course dinners with Malbec-vs-Patagonian-pinot flights — one of the city''s oldest supper clubs","commission":"DMC-brokered / direct"},{"name":"Malbec / Argentine-wine tasting","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"comfort","source":"https://theculturetrip.com/south-america/argentina/articles/the-best-closed-door-restaurants-in-buenos-aires","hook":"Guided verticals of Mendoza Malbec, Patagonian pinot, and high-altitude Salta torrontés — in-city tasting rooms or a DMC-curated flight","si":"culinary","blurb":"Guided verticals of Mendoza Malbec, Patagonian pinot, and high-altitude Salta torrontés — in-city tasting rooms or a DMC-curated flight","commission":"DMC / activities affiliate"},{"name":"San Telmo Sunday feria (Calle Defensa)","si_tag":"Culinary / Culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Buenos_Aires","hook":"The Sunday street market and antiques fair — empanadas, choripán, street tango, and browsing","si":"Culinary / Culture","blurb":"The Sunday street market and antiques fair — empanadas, choripán, street tango, and browsing","commission":"content-led; guided-tour affiliate"},{"name":"MALBA — Latin American art museum","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Buenos_Aires/Palermo_%26_Recoleta","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"admission non-commissionable; DMC guided visit"},{"name":"Teatro Colon guided tour / opera night","si_tag":"Culture / RHN","tier":"essential","source":"https://turismo.buenosaires.gob.ar/en","si":"Culture / RHN","commission":"box-office non-commissionable; DMC package"},{"name":"Palermo Soho boutiques","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Buenos_Aires/Palermo_%26_Recoleta","hook":"High-end Argentine fashion and leather boutiques on cobblestone streets — the \"silk\" half of BA''s soul","si":"culture","blurb":"High-end Argentine fashion and leather boutiques on cobblestone streets — the \"silk\" half of BA''s soul","commission":"content-led; concierge personal-shopper"},{"name":"La Boca / Caminito (daytime only)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://solsalute.com/blog/is-buenos-aires-safe-for-tourists/","hook":"The painted tin tenements, birthplace of tango and of Boca Juniors — a guided daytime visit only","si":"culture","blurb":"The painted tin tenements, birthplace of tango and of Boca Juniors — a guided daytime visit only","commission":"guided-tour affiliate / DMC"},{"name":"Tigre Delta day","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://luxurylatinamerica.com/blog/2023/03/13/day-trips-from-buenos-aires/","hook":"An hour north, the Paraná Delta''s maze of channels and stilt-houses","si":"culture","blurb":"An hour north, the Paraná Delta''s maze of channels and stilt-houses","commission":"activities affiliate / DMC day-tour"},{"name":"Pampas estancia day — San Antonio de Areco (gaucho)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://solsalute.com/blog/best-buenos-aires-day-trips/","hook":"~1½ hrs out onto the grasslands to a working ranch: horseback, all-afternoon asado, folklore, and gaucho tradition","si":"culture","blurb":"~1½ hrs out onto the grasslands to a working ranch: horseback, all-afternoon asado, folklore, and gaucho tradition","commission":"DMC / MoR estancia booking"},{"name":"Argentine Open Polo (November, Palermo)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.theaircharterjournal.com/air-charter-journal/argentine-polo-open-2025","hook":"The world''s most prestigious polo championship, at the \"Cathedral of Polo\" — grandstand and hospitality seats are a marquee November draw","si":"culture","blurb":"The world''s most prestigious polo championship, at the \"Cathedral of Polo\" — grandstand and hospitality seats are a marquee November draw","commission":"DMC / hospitality-package MoR"},{"name":"Colonia del Sacramento day trip (Uruguay)","si_tag":"culture","tier":"comfort","source":"https://luxurylatinamerica.com/blog/2023/03/13/day-trips-from-buenos-aires/","hook":"Ferry across the Río de la Plata to a UNESCO colonial town — the calm counterpoint to BA","si":"culture","blurb":"Ferry across the Río de la Plata to a UNESCO colonial town — the calm counterpoint to BA","commission":"ferry affiliate + DMC day-tour"}],"faq":[{"q":"When is the best time to visit Buenos Aires for a honeymoon?","a":"The spring and fall shoulders — October–November and March–April — are the sweet spot, with mild 18–26 °C days and thinner crowds than the hot, humid summer. November is the standout: the jacarandas bloom lilac across Recoleta''s boulevards and the Argentine Open Polo fills Palermo, so treat November premium beds as a 3–6 month advance book.","source":"lonelyplanet.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What are the must-see cultural sites in Buenos Aires?","a":"Start with Recoleta Cemetery — 6,400+ statues and crypts, including Evita Perón''s tomb, with free Spanish guided tours Tue–Sun — then Teatro Colón, one of the great opera houses of the world, and a daytime visit to La Boca''s Caminito, birthplace of tango. San Telmo''s Sunday feria on Calle Defensa rounds out the heritage circuit.","source":"buenosairesfreewalks.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What is a puerta cerrada (closed-door) restaurant?","a":"They are secret chef''s-home supper clubs, a Porteño institution. Fogón Asado runs a Michelin-recommended 9-course asado tasting for ~35 guests with optional Argentine wine pairings, while Casa Saltshaker (est. 2005) does intimate shared-table five-course dinners with Malbec-vs-Patagonian-pinot flights — one of the city''s oldest such houses.","source":"theculturetrip.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Buenos Aires?","a":"Snatch-and-grab theft, not violence. BA''s characteristic street crime is motochorros (motorcycle thieves) and distraction scams, with roughly 90% of motochorro snatchings happening at traffic lights; keep your phone off café-table edges and use vetted radio-taxi or ride-apps. La Boca is daytime-and-Caminito only — arrive by taxi and leave before dark.","source":"secretsofbuenosaires.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Do I need travel insurance for Argentina?","a":"Treat it as required and always buy it. Under Decree 366/2025, effective 2025-07-01, non-resident travelers were required to carry travel medical insurance covering emergency care, hospitalization, evacuation and repatriation, with airlines confirming at check-in. One December-2025 secondary source reported the rule may have been suspended or modified (unverified and conflicting), so verify current enforcement at booking.","source":"globalrescue.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Buenos Aires Travel Guide — Tango, Steak & Boutique Hotels | TravelWell","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","search_language":"es-AR","long_tail_en":["things to do in Buenos Aires","best tango show Buenos Aires","closed-door restaurants Buenos Aires","Buenos Aires honeymoon","best time to visit Buenos Aires","Recoleta cemetery Evita","Tigre Delta day trip","San Antonio de Areco estancia","Buenos Aires luxury hotels","is Buenos Aires safe"],"local_keywords":["qué hacer en Buenos Aires","show de tango Buenos Aires","mejores parrillas Buenos Aires","puertas cerradas Buenos Aires","Cementerio de la Recoleta Evita","estancia San Antonio de Areco","escapada al Delta del Tigre","hoteles de lujo Buenos Aires","Abierto Argentino de Polo","mejor época para visitar Buenos Aires"],"hreflang":["en","es-AR"]},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Four Seasons Hotel Buenos Aires + La Mansion","barrio":"Recoleta","tier":"ultra","earning":"FS Preferred Partner / Virtuoso — commission + amenities (UNVERIFIED %)"},{"name":"Alvear Palace Hotel","barrio":"Recoleta","tier":"ultra","earning":"Virtuoso / LHW — commission + amenities (UNVERIFIED %)"},{"name":"Palacio Duhau — Park Hyatt Buenos Aires","barrio":"Recoleta","tier":"ultra","earning":"Hyatt Prive / Virtuoso — commission + amenities (UNVERIFIED %)"},{"name":"Faena Hotel Buenos Aires","barrio":"Puerto Madero","tier":"ultra","earning":"Virtuoso / brand luxury — commission + amenities (UNVERIFIED %)"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Buenos Aires, Argentina, Argentina"},"geo":{"lat":-34.6037,"lng":-58.3816}}'::jsonb, 39)
