Nov-Mar","commission":"bundle into guided evening; ticket non-commissionable pass-through"},{"name":"Fuerte de San Miguel — Museo Arqueológico de Campeche","si_tag":"CLT","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/mexico/yucatan-peninsula/campeche/attractions/museo-arqueologico-de-campeche-fuerte-de-san-miguel/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"guided half-day + transfer margin; entry non-commissionable"},{"name":"Edzná Maya ruins (52 km SE)","si_tag":"CLT","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.themayanruinswebsite.com/edzna.html","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","when":"year-round","commission":"guided archaeology day tour (DMC/affiliate) + site fee pass-through"},{"name":"Xtacumbilxunaán caves (near Bolonchén)","si_tag":"CLT","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/mexico/attractions/grutas-de-xtacumbilxunaan/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"guided day tour (commissionable) + entry pass-through"},{"name":"Isla Aguada / Isla del Carmen dolphin encounter","si_tag":"romance","tier":"comfort","source":"https://en-yucatan.com/campeche/isla-aguada/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Open-water small-boat operation, sun exposure, weather turns Guided only Confirm life vests on board and worn, weather-check the launch, no touching/chasing dolphins, motion-sickness prep","si":"romance","blurb":"Open-water small-boat operation, sun exposure, weather turns Guided only Confirm life vests on board and worn, weather-check the launch, no touching/chasing dolphins, motion-sickness prep","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"licensed sanctuary boat tour via affiliate (GetYourGuide/Civitatis) or DMC"},{"name":"The Malecón at sunset (7 km Gulf-front)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.lonelyplanet.com/mexico/yucatan-peninsula/campeche/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"romance","when":"year-round","commission":"free amenity selling boutique-hotel package"},{"name":"Candlelit colonial-courtyard dining","si_tag":"romance","tier":"premier","source":"https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotels/cpehl-hacienda-puerta-campeche-a-luxury-collection-hotel-campeche/overview/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"hotel F&B + room commission"},{"name":"Pan de cazón (state dish)","si_tag":"CUL","tier":"essential","source":"https://mexiconewsdaily.com/lifestyle/food/state-by-plate-campeches-pan-de-cazon/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Campechano cuisine is one of Mexico''s most distinct regional tables","si":"culinary","blurb":"Campechano cuisine is one of Mexico''s most distinct regional tables","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"guided food walk / cooking class (tour affiliate)"},{"name":"Pámpano en escabeche & coctel campechano","si_tag":"CUL","tier":"essential","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/campeche-food-guide/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"curated dining list + food tour / market visit"},{"name":"Calakmul gateway (own dossier)","si_tag":"CLT","tier":"premier","source":"https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/895/","timing":"Nov-Mar","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the deep-jungle Maya megacity + biosphere is a long day/overnight from Campeche City and should not be collapsed into this file","si":"culture","blurb":"the deep-jungle Maya megacity + biosphere is a long day/overnight from Campeche City and should not be collapsed into this file","when":"Nov-Mar","commission":"multi-day DMC program from Campeche City"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is there to see in the walled city?","a":"The UNESCO centro itself: a 17th-century wall (1686–1704), eight bastions, a checkerboard grid and 1,000+ colonial buildings painted ochre, coral and mint — walk Calle 59 at golden hour. At night, the Puerta de Tierra sound-and-light show projects four centuries of pirate history onto the Land Gate for about US$5.","source":"whc.unesco.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Edzná worth a day trip from Campeche?","a":"Yes — it is the region''s under-visited Maya highlight. Edzná, 52 km southeast, is a major Maya capital whose five-story pyramid rises ~40 m and blends Puuc, Chenes and Petén styles, with a rare ancient hydraulic canal system and a fraction of Chichén Itzá''s crowds. Go at the 8 AM opening to beat the heat.","source":"themayanruinswebsite.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Campeche good for a couple''s trip?","a":"Yes, as a slow, characterful pause. Dinner in a restored-hacienda courtyard (La Guardia at Hacienda Puerta Campeche), a rooftop pool at an 18th-century mansion, and the peninsula''s best sunset along the 7-km malecón make it a honeymoon-adjacent \"second city,\" most often paired with Mérida (~2.5 hr) as a 2–3 night add-on.","source":"lonelyplanet.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What should I eat in Campeche?","a":"Start with pan de cazón — the state dish of layered tortillas, black beans, shredded dogfish and tomato-habanero sauce. Add pámpano en escabeche (colonial-era pompano in bitter-orange escabeche) and the coctel campechano seafood cocktail, with Gulf catch landed the same morning.","source":"mexiconewsdaily.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Campeche?","a":"Heat and thin flight schedules, not crime. The exposed ruins at Edzná and the treeless malecón are hot at midday — hat, high SPF, water and early site visits. Campeche''s own airport (CPE) is thinly served, so most travelers fly into Mérida (MID) and drive ~2.5 hr; drink bottled water only and use repellent for dengue in the rainy season (Jun–Oct).","source":"climatestotravel.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Campeche City, Mexico — The Walled UNESCO Pastel Port | TravelWell.World","search_language":"es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Campeche","ciudad amurallada Campeche","Edzná zona arqueológica","hoteles boutique centro histórico Campeche","avistamiento de delfines Isla Aguada","pan de cazón Campeche","Carnaval de Campeche fechas"],"long_tail_en":["is Campeche City Mexico safe","things to do in Campeche walled city","Edzná ruins day trip from Campeche","Isla Aguada dolphin tour Campeche","best boutique hotels Campeche historic center"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","primary_keyword":"Campeche City"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"romance","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"property":"Hacienda Puerta Campeche, a Luxury Collection Hotel","brand":"Marriott — Luxury Collection","rooms":14,"positioning":"Restored 16th-c. haciendas; the destination''s true luxury ceiling","earning":"Marriott commissionable; Luxury Collection eligible for Marriott STARS/Luxury consortia — verify FHR/amenity status at booking","mor":"hotel-direct commission","tier":"$$$$"},{"property":"Casa Don Gustavo Boutique Hotel","rooms":10,"positioning":"Restored 18th-c. mansion, rooftop pool, pedestrian center","earning":"Independent — direct / bedbank / consortia","mor":"hotel-direct or platform","tier":"$$$"},{"property":"Hotel H177","positioning":"Boutique centro property, Calle 59","earning":"Independent boutique; direct / affiliate","mor":"hotel-direct or platform","tier":"comfort"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Campeche City, Mexico, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":19.845,"lng":-90.523}}'::jsonb, 41),
